te\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1508638#post1508638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welp, it is go time, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know judging a book by the cover is something we're not supposed to do. But this cover is so beautiful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T08:34:29-07:00","id":1508640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1508639#post1508639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know judging a book by the cover is something we're not supposed to do. But this cover is so beautiful</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is, and it uses the elements I love about WtA; The forest vs its destruction.<br /> <br /> Given how HEAVILY the forest imagery is used vs the stated focus, I'm guessing the cover is not matching the insides XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T08:38:52-07:00","id":1508641,"title":"","content":"I will be passing on this. Not to crap on anyone else who might legitimately like the changes and focus of this &quot;reimagining&quot;, but it strays too far from the game I know and love to be interested in it personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T08:39:16-07:00","id":1508642,"title":"","content":"I like the cover as well but I'm far more curious about finally getting a glimpse at the mechanics of this game on Thursday.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the blurb does offer some insight into the premise of W5 (or, I guess, just confirms stuff we've already heard last year):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaia is dying.<br /> <br /> The ices melt, while the seas swell.<br /> <br /> The heat rises, while the forests wither.<br /> <br /> Extinction threatens millions, in favor of the few.<br /> <br /> The Garou \u2014 warlike shapeshifters torn be\u00adtween Rage and spirit, between Wolf and Man, and champions of the earth-mother \u2014 have failed.<br /> <br /> The Apocalypse is here.<br /> <br /> Yet, a new generation of Garou now call upon their Rage to confront the forces of destruction, avarice, and greed ravaging the earth-mother. With tooth and claw the Garou will wrest her from the brink of death \u2014 or follow her enemies to the grave.<br /> <br /> Will you answer their howl?<br /> <br /> What legends will the Garou sing of you?<br /> <br /> When will you Rage?<br /> <br /> Features:<ul><li>As a new generation Garou, you will confront the forces of destruction, avarice, and greed ravaging the earth-mother.</li> <li>Utilize the 5th edition Storyteller system to create your chronicles within the World of Darkness.</li> <li>Includes everything you need to know to build your own character or guide a troupe as they explore their new forms.</li> <li>As a werewolf, build your legend, vie for renown, and fight to take back what has been lost.</li> <li>Join one of eleven tribes, each unique and rich with narrative depth for players to explore, and Storytellers to utilize.</li> <li>This 300+ page hardcover book also includes an introductory story to guide new Werewolf players and veteran World of Darkness enthusiasts through their first game.\u200b</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>There's some new info, though. The book has 300+ pages (in comparison, V5 (extended version) has 430 pages and H5 has 288 pages). But of course that's minus all the stuff that got covered in the Expanded Mechanics pdf. And I guess the premise really seems to rely on the idea that the reason the Garou-PCs are better than the older Garou who have failed is that they're &quot;a new generation&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T08:43:20-07:00","id":1508643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1508641#post1508641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will be passing on this. Not to crap on anyone else who might legitimately like the changes and focus of this &quot;reimagining&quot;, but it strays too far from the game I know and love to be interested in it personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Super respect that. And I'd like to take a moment to apologize for moemnts in the past where I didn't respected that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T09:09:28-07:00","id":1508644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1508641#post1508641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will be passing on this. Not to crap on anyone else who might legitimately like the changes and focus of this &quot;reimagining&quot;, but it strays too far from the game I know and love to be interested in it personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna play wait and see. If it has ideas and mechanics I can use I might grab it but I'm not taking any more leaps of faith after v5 anarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T10:14:19-07:00","id":1508649,"title":"","content":"Are we migrating the discussion of W5 to this thread or are we going to keep it over in the Q&amp;A one?<br /> <br /> I don't really see myself buying it but I am curious on what it says from a morbid angle.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T11:39:10-07:00","id":1508659,"title":"","content":"I loved the cover, but I also think it's a huge mistake. The claws on the sides of the image should absolutely not be there given the Internet and memes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T21:22:24-07:00","id":1508709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1508659#post1508659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I loved the cover, but I also think it's a huge mistake. The claws on the sides of the image should absolutely not be there given the Internet and memes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Took me a minute to get that one, made me chuckle once I did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T23:57:56-07:00","id":1508713,"title":"","content":"According to someone on the rpg.net thread on the same topic, Outstar mentioned that the Fianna got renamed. Hopefully the GoF did as well, but...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1508709#post1508709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Took me a minute to get that one, made me chuckle once I did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf: the Goatse.cx","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T01:13:46-07:00","id":1508718,"title":"","content":"Just a fair warning (and why I didn't just say that): For anyone that's managed to avoid goatse, it is an old and <b>incredibly</b> NSFW meme. Many people will want some brain bleach handy if you decide to go look up what on Earth we're talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T01:48:02-07:00","id":1508722,"title":"","content":"I must confess that while I know what goatse is it didn't occur to me seeing the cover.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T02:16:46-07:00","id":1508724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1508718#post1508718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a fair warning (and why I didn't just say that): For anyone that's managed to avoid goatse, it is an old and <b>incredibly</b> NSFW meme. Many people will want some brain bleach handy if you decide to go look up what on Earth we're talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually half expecting people to just use the claws and the opening to insert varied different images any day now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T07:48:54-07:00","id":1508749,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, slightly bigger than H5 which is a book with very little meat on its bones and a lot of wasted page space + the Core integrates an introductory scenario......maybe they removed all the culture and background because there was no room for it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T10:36:47-07:00","id":1508764,"title":"","content":"I'll probably skip for now, but if it turns out to be closer to V5 than H5 in quality I'll probably pick it up close to Christmas (like I might pick H5 up at some point this year). Got a lot more CofD and Storypath stuff I want to prioritise first though.<br /> <br /> As for the size, low 300 pages is about the size of Requiem, Forsaken, and Vigil 2e, and a bit smaller than Deviant. Combined with some of the rules being in a pdf that means there's plenty of space for lore. It just depends on the designers to actually put it in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T15:45:35-07:00","id":1508788,"title":"","content":"The cover is really nice. I'm holding off on this, too. If anyone gets the PDF when it's released and wants to do a WIR thread, I'd read the heck out of that, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T16:01:27-07:00","id":1508789,"title":"","content":"I really like where the cover was clearly trying to go... just... memes.<br /> <br /> That said, I am hoping the art in W5 keeps up the quality of H5. I might not like the contents that much, but if people are going to pay coffee-table book prices, they should get a book that's pretty to go with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T01:37:04-07:00","id":1508865,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it seems like it's similar to H5 where it's this mix of black and white with gold to emphasize things but here instead of gold it's red.<br /> <br /> Also, previous covers (both for V5 and H5) were done by Tomas Arfert (who's also the Art Director of the WOD-team), but this cover is from Krzysztof Bieniawski (who also did interior art for the H5 book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T08:36:04-07:00","id":1509037,"title":"","content":"Vote on each tribe will get a preview of their 5th edition version<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYqhnlri-lFU9HG4gUb0fEyuMY_DEi9CNN3Dc-t6ev6P--GA/viewform?usp=sf_link\u200b\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYqhnlri-lFU9HG4gUb0fEyuMY_DEi9CNN3Dc-t6ev6P--GA/viewform?usp=sf_link\u200b\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYqhnlri-lFU9HG4gUb0fEyuMY_DEi9CNN3Dc-t6ev6P--GA/viewform?usp=sf_link\u200b\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYqhnlri-lFU9HG4gUb0fEyuMY_DEi9CNN3Dc-t6ev6P--GA/viewform?usp=sf_link\u200b </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T10:29:26-07:00","id":1509058,"title":"","content":"Ok, so Fianna are Hart Wardens......Deer Guardians.....fits with the Patron at least...but it feels a little thrown together when you say it outloud....could just be unfamiliarity.<br /> <br /> Damn no option for Fenrir or Stargazers there, much as I don't want to boost engagement I do kinda want to know what a tribe even is in W5 other than a bunch of isolated scattered Garou that follow the same Patron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T11:44:51-07:00","id":1509072,"title":"","content":"I have watched the preview and summarized the new stuff. Two things first, though: One, a big part of the preview is that it was accompanied by the pages of the actual introduction, so there are sections where Outstar is just reading out loud what is said on those pages. The pages can be found on the pre-order-page for the W5-corebook on the Renegade-store-webpage. Two, what I do note in relation to each section is the commentary Outstar adds and I note every time there's a page-break.<br /> <br /> Okay, so here's the written summary (same deal as usual: I try to stay as close to the phrasing Outstar uses and there's no commentary from me in here):<ul><li>Outstar was one of the STs for the playtests and for that they ran an introductory-campaign (written by Chrisopher Chung (not sure if I understood the name correctly) ) which will also be included in the W5 corebook.</li> <li>There will be a series of previews over the coming weeks.</li> <li>This first preview is about the introduction.</li> <li>We-howl-bit/pg7 (as in-character introduction): From Outstar: This is how Werewolf the fifth edition starts. This is the Apocalypse. The Apocalypse has already happened or it\u2019s happening right now.</li> <li>First introduction page/pg9: Emphasis on the section at the bottom right about how W5 is a re-imagining, not a continuation.</li> <li>W5 is partially about returning to the roots of 1st edition and partially being its own thing.</li> <li>Section beginning at upper left: The first paragraph sums up the premise of the game.</li> <li>Those who come from VtM, the same way vampires might try to do good and it doesn\u2019t work, it\u2019s similar with werewolves. The motivations of werewolves are overall selfless/unegoistic but the way they pursue may not be so good.</li> <li>Werewolves want to preserve and protect Gaia, slow down the ongoing Apocalypse or fight back despite a world that is assumed to be lost already.</li> <li>Compared to playing a vampire, the playtesters (some of them were vampire-players) said to Outstar: As werewolves they felt like they were more \u201cactionable\u201d, they have powers that allow them to fight back. But they might not be able to stop the Apocalypse from happening. It feels powerful to play a Werewolf, though.</li> <li>Werwolf is much more a game about action and you being able to do something.</li> <li>Spirituality bit at the bottom-right: The Triad is still there, you fight the Wyrm</li> <li>Werewolf the Apocalypse Truths/pg10: Werwolves don\u2019t fully belong to the spirit-world or the the human world.</li> <li>Rage is similar in concept to Hunger (from V5) but works differently.</li> <li>Werewolves don\u2019t talk to Gaia or get missions from her. Each werewolf has their own interpretation of what protecting Gaia exactly means.</li> <li>Talking about how Garou want to confront agents of the Wyrm \u201creal or imagined: This is because Garou are not the good guys necessarily. It\u2019s still a World of Darkness with a lot of shades of grey.</li> <li>The same way trying to be a good guy as a Vampire is hard with the Beast trying to put you down, as a Werewolf you\u2019re also struggling to do good because of Rage and your ways may not be the good ways.</li> <li>What do Werewolves do?/pg11: \u201cTaking back what has been lost\u201d (as the first point) can be a physical fight but can also be a metaphorical fight. Water may be polluted and we as humans are sometimes not aware of this but werewolves are.</li> <li>Second point is \u201cbuilding your own legend\u201d: This ties to the Renown-mechanic which allows you to use Gifts and Rites.</li> <li>Third point is \u201cexploring the mysteries of the Umbra\u201d: Players can enter it from any place to see the spiritual reflection of the world.</li> <li>For example, players want to do a heist on a bank and they want to get inside a corporate building and the players want to know what the building looks like in the Umbra. And the ST can use this opportunity to paint a picture</li> <li>Fourth point is \u201clooking for others of their kind\u201d: Kin are potential and sometimes actual werewolves who haven\u2019t been accepted into Garou society yet. And it\u2019s important for Kinseeking Garou to look for them. Because Kin might be doing bad stuff because they have no self-control or understanding of what they are.</li> <li>As a WOD-game W5 is very story-driven but you can make them more action-focused. Though, at the core the game values storytelling more than mechanics and rolling.</li> <li>When Outstar was a player in a playtest, she and the other players really pushed the mechanics and shifted into Crinos-form as much as possible and so the game was heavy on action.</li> <li>When Outstar was the ST for the playtest, she wanted to players to use the Crinos-form (or \u201cthe nuclear option\u201d as they nicknamed it during the playtest) but they avoided using it until late in the story.</li> <li>Mature Content Warning/pg13, forms of playing and playing aids get discussed.</li> <li>Lexicon: Instead of Humanity you have Harano and Hauglosk trackers. Rage-Dice function like Desperation-Dice in Hunter but with different flavor.</li> <li>Fianna are now called Hart Wardens.</li> <li>There\u2019s a google-doc with a poll about which Tribe should get previewed first.</li> <li>Q&amp;A-section:</li> <li>The W5 physical book is on different paper than the V5 corebook, not as white, not glossy.</li> <li>Final corrected version of V5 Players Guide will get released soon as well.</li> <li>Crinos as a form is tied to Rage (previews will cover that later).</li> <li>Next preview in two weeks.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T12:22:22-07:00","id":1509077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509072#post1509072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have watched the preview and summarized the new stuff. Two things first, though: One, a big part of the preview is that it was accompanied by the pages of the actual introduction, so there are sections where Outstar is just reading out loud what is said on those pages. The pages can be found on the pre-order-page for the W5-corebook on the Renegade-store-webpage. Two, what I do note in relation to each section is the commentary Outstar adds and I note every time there's a page-break.<br /> <br /> Okay, so here's the written summary (same deal as usual: I try to stay as close to the phrasing Outstar uses and there's no commentary from me in here):<ul><li>Outstar was one of the STs for the playtests and for that they ran an introductory-campaign (written by Chrisopher Chung (not sure if I understood the name correc