....Deer Guardians.....fits with the Patron at least...but it feels a little thrown together when you say it outloud....could just be unfamiliarity.<br /> <br /> Damn no option for Fenrir or Stargazers there, much as I don't want to boost engagement I do kinda want to know what a tribe even is in W5 other than a bunch of isolated scattered Garou that follow the same Patron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fenrir need to have their name changed, too, for the same reasons the Fianna got a name change. Or to simply just not have ever existed in this iteration, but, you know, they kept insisting on it. Hopefully they at least changed the glyph...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T13:06:37-07:00","id":1509082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509079#post1509079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fenrir need to have their name changed, too, for the same reasons the Fianna got a name change. Or to simply just not have ever existed in this iteration, but, you know, they kept insisting on it. Hopefully they at least changed the glyph...</div> </div> </div> </div>With none of the &quot; Tribes&quot; having ties to human culture would the Fenrir just be Wolfs Children or something similar? The Glyph will be changed, pity they prevented OPP from change it in the latter half of W20.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T13:08:05-07:00","id":1509083,"title":"","content":"Considering the earlier previews had four of the otherwise unchanged Tribes have significant redesigns of their glyphs, and the two that were getting name changes from the get go got new glyphs, it's hard to imagine we're not going to see a GoF glyph redesign too. The Hart Wardens could probably use a new one that makes more sense with the new name, but I could understand not spending the resources on it at this point (though really, the Silver Fang one is the only major redesign that I actually can at least understand what the point is)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T13:15:46-07:00","id":1509084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509083#post1509083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the earlier previews had four of the otherwise unchanged Tribes have significant redesigns of their glyphs, and the two that were getting name changes from the get go got new glyphs, it's hard to imagine we're not going to see a GoF glyph redesign too. The Hart Wardens could probably use a new one that makes more sense with the new name, but I could understand not spending the resources on it at this point (though really, the Silver Fang one is the only major redesign that I actually can at least understand what the point is)..</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Most of the other 're-designs' are &quot; lets make it more complicated with this little squiggle for no reason.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T13:24:17-07:00","id":1509086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509077#post1509077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for doing that so we didn't have to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ok, so pretty much nothing more than whats on the pages.....and they still can't decide whether the Apocalypse has happened or not and or if Gaia is dead or not......I have a feeling different freelancers had different interpretations of the vagaries....so that will be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tone from back in October when Justin Achilli was talking about this was certainly very different compared to how Outstar talked about it now. The word &quot;action&quot; in the sense of &quot;doing something about the situation you're in&quot; came up a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509077#post1509077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chris Chung is a fairly well known board game designer, could it be him?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first name was definitely Christopher but I'm not sure about the surname. Once the book comes out the credits-page will certainly help.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T13:38:18-07:00","id":1509087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509086#post1509086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tone from back in October when Justin Achilli was talking about this was certainly very different compared to how Outstar talked about it now. The word &quot;action&quot; in the sense of &quot;doing something about the situation you're in&quot; came up a lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> The first name was definitely Christopher but I'm not sure about the surname. Once the book comes out the credits-page will certainly help.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It could just be that Justin was/is not great at communicating his ideas or that things were reworked after October, we know there was still ongoing playtesting at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T13:45:51-07:00","id":1509088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509087#post1509087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could just be that Justin was/is not great at communicating his ideas or that things were reworked after October, we know there was still ongoing playtesting at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>We will never know what exactly happened behind the scenes there between October and early January when we learned that he had left the WOD-team to do something else (and the rest of the work on the W5 book would be done without him).<br /> <br /> And I mean we just have to look at the Fianna/Hart Wardens-Tribe: In October during the Discord Q&amp;A somebody asked him about it and JA dismissed it by saying &quot;Fianna's just a word.&quot; - and well, now we have a new name for the Tribe. So who knows what went on behind the scenes there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T13:51:37-07:00","id":1509089,"title":"","content":"Anyway I'll stop using the J word lest I accidentally summon Young Master Dawkins yet again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T14:16:15-07:00","id":1509095,"title":"","content":"A new concept that wasn't mentioned by Outstar but I noticed on the Lexicon-Page:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaia's Howl: An audible indicator (capable of sometimes affecting other senses) of the age of Apocalypse, perceptible only by Garou and perhaps some spirits. </div> </div> </div>If it's indeed <i>Gaia</i>'s Howl then this would mean in W5 Gaia has communicated with the Garou. It's strange, though, that only Garou and &quot;perhaps some other spirits&quot; are mentioned here (shouldn't it be all the various shifters that serve Gaia...?). And I still can't quite understand why the Get need to be antagonists from an in-game-standpoint. Raging out because it's the &quot;Age Of Apocalypse&quot; while your culture's holy mission had been all about preventing that doesn't sound that insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T14:23:00-07:00","id":1509096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509095#post1509095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A new concept that wasn't mentioned by Outstar but I noticed on the Lexicon-Page:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If it's indeed <i>Gaia</i>'s Howl then this would mean in W5 Gaia has communicated with the Garou. It's strange, though, that only Garou and &quot;perhaps some other spirits&quot; are mentioned here (shouldn't it be all the various shifters that serve Gaia...?). And I still can't quite understand why the Get need to be antagonists from an in-game-standpoint. Raging out because it's the &quot;Age Of Apocalypse&quot; while your culture's holy mission had been all about preventing that doesn't sound that insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf, if it were written under the influence of Dementation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T15:05:06-07:00","id":1509105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509086#post1509086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tone from back in October when Justin Achilli was talking about this was certainly very different compared to how Outstar talked about it now. The word &quot;action&quot; in the sense of &quot;doing something about the situation you're in&quot; came up a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't Renegade working on a version of W5 before Justin was given it? I wonder how much of this is Justin's book and how much is their previous version. I suspect we'll never know, but I wouldn't be shocked if they have dug up some pre-JA lore and mechanics to give it a more proactive tone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T17:56:14-07:00","id":1509121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509079#post1509079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fenrir need to have their name changed, too, for the same reasons the Fianna got a name change. Or to simply just not have ever existed in this iteration, but, you know, they kept insisting on it. Hopefully they at least changed the glyph...</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally... or perhaps it's ok for Scandinavian cultures to be put in a villainous position for them... who knows...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T18:13:16-07:00","id":1509124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenixpp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509121#post1509121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally... or perhaps it's ok for Scandinavian cultures to be put in a villainous position for them... who knows...</div> </div> </div> </div>...The Get themselves kind of held Scandinavian cultures as villainous, on account of all that Odin worship and all. He was their nemesis, and they almost certainly spent a lot of time and energy killing the most devout worshipers of the Aesir and Vanir. Up until Christianity rolled in, at which point they sat back and watched the fireworks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T22:26:54-07:00","id":1509135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When Outstar was the ST for the playtest, she wanted to players to use the Crinos-form (or \u201cthe nuclear option\u201d as they nicknamed it during the playtest) but they avoided using it until late in the story. </div> </div> </div>See, THIS is what I meant by the crinos limit being bad. Gauru was rarely if ever used in Forsaken games I was in BECAUSE of the time limit. And that to me is a shame, because one of the best parts of WtA power was how <i>natural </i>the crinos form was. It was a form of war but also a form of rituals and spiritualism. Put a limit on it and suddenly it becomes something to be avoided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T22:45:28-07:00","id":1509137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509124#post1509124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...The Get themselves kind of held Scandinavian cultures as villainous, on account of all that Odin worship and all. He was their nemesis, and they almost certainly spent a lot of time and energy killing the most devout worshipers of the Aesir and Vanir. Up until Christianity rolled in, at which point they sat back and watched the fireworks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but I was referring to the Devs. After all their talk to respect cultures and severing the Garou tribal links to them in order to do so. We still have a greek totem and a tribe with a norse entity in the name and as their Incarna (most likely).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T22:52:28-07:00","id":1509138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509087#post1509087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could just be that Justin was/is not great at communicating his ideas or that things were reworked after October, we know there was still ongoing playtesting at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's more a general cultural trend in wod public interactions across the board than any individual writter. I've noticed that the games often do odd design decisions or even bad ones then articulate their justification in odd ways. For example because they don't like Sabbat play they'll use phrases like 'dark mirror of the carmarilla' to derride Sabbat play in revised and 2nd end or 'medieval death cult' to justify how 2d they are now. Or 'v5 is about personal horror' to justify pretty much anything. All of which fall apart when you think on it but sound good initially.<br /> <br /> werewolfs had a couple of in differant public statements from differant sources with this issue (eg weird descriptions of tribes as a a handful of words) and it's hard to follow their mindset because I'm unsure of the internal logic and I'm not even convinced its the actual reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 04-21-2023, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T23:59:45-07:00","id":1509140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509135#post1509135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, THIS is what I meant by the crinos limit being bad. Gauru was rarely if ever used in Forsaken games I was in BECAUSE of the time limit. And that to me is a shame, because one of the best parts of WtA power was how <i>natural </i>the crinos form was. It was a form of war but also a form of rituals and spiritualism. Put a limit on it and suddenly it becomes something to be avoided.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I also immediately thought of that... What I also could envision for how this could work is that in Crinos Form you <i>have to</i> add a higher-than-usual amount of Rage Dice to <i>every </i>action and so while getting big dice-pools you're always in danger of triggering Rage and losing control of yourself. And the way they phrased it in the previews was how it's all about &quot;Unless you want to physically destroy stuff, Rage is bad.&quot;. So I could imagine the avoidance could come from it working like that. And that only in obvious moments like confronting the &quot;big bad&quot; of the chronicle where players care less enough about the consequences of &quot;raging out&quot; to use the Crinos Form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T02:17:06-07:00","id":1509152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509140#post1509140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I also immediately thought of that... What I also could envision for how this could work is that in Crinos Form you <i>have to</i> add a higher-than-usual amount of Rage Dice to <i>every </i>action and so while getting big dice-pools you're always in danger of triggering Rage and losing control of yourself. And the way they phrased it in the previews was how it's all about &quot;Unless you want to physically destroy stuff, Rage is bad.&quot;. So I could imagine the avoidance could come from it working like that. And that only in obvious moments like confronting the &quot;big bad&quot; of the chronicle where players care less enough about the consequences of &quot;raging out&quot; to use the Crinos Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, extra Rage dice were already a thing in WtA (crinos form has a lower frenzy threshold) and your suggestion works better.<br /> <br /> The limit on crinos/gauru is also really killing the thematic feeling of werewolf, because you DO want people to use it. If using it feels too risky in 90% of situations AND you might lose control over the character if you stay in it too long, though? The players often prefer to take less power for more control. Thus, the form on all the covers and promo art is relegated to an unwanted event in Frenzy/Death Rage cases.<br /> <br /> In Forsaken, as the focus is more smaller scale, this is more in terms of its themes. But still, players should WANT to use crinos and WANT to go full werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T03:30:13-07:00","id":1509160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509152#post1509152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, extra Rage dice were already a thing in WtA (crinos form has a lower frenzy threshold) and your suggestion works better.<br /> <br /> The limit on crinos/gauru is also really killing the thematic feeling of werewolf, because you DO want people to use it. If using it feels too risky in 90% of situations AND you might lose control over the character if you stay in it too long, though? The players often prefer to take less power for more control. Thus, the form on all the covers and promo art is relegated to an unwanted event in Frenzy/Death Rage cases.<br /> <br /> In Forsaken, as the focus is more smaller scale, this is more in terms of its themes. But still, players should WANT to use crinos and WANT to go full werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>In relation to that, I'm also still not sure why the Get then are this bad Tribe that has left the Garou Nation or was kicked out (depending on what the lore will be exactly). Sure, they have embraced the Rage but the way it's described all Garou are struggling with being ticking Rage-bombs in this setup whether they want to or not. If the Get are accused of going too far with their violence, I mean, all Garou are one bad Rage-Dice-roll away from going too far with the violence. And Get being too hasty and paranoid (kinda like &quot;you're either with me or against me.&quot;) is similar to the general idea in the introduction of werewolves &quot;wanting to confront the agents of the Wyrm, real or imagined.&quot; The only real difference we've gotten through the previews is that they're permanently locked into Hauglosk. Remove that and I still don't see why they couldn't have just been another Tribe with a different outlook on Rage and a more aggressive tact when it comes to fighting the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T04:53:12-07:00","id":1509166,"title":"","content":"Tbf the big limit on Gauru isn't the time limit (it's short, but CofD combat is fast and it is lore-wise meant to be only for killing), it's the fact that it doesn't let you act tactically. For the Uratha their wolf-man form is a tool, which fits with the fact that they're human/spirit hybrids, not human/wolf hybrids.<br /> <br /> Plus some can assume Gauru without the associated rage anyway, even if it does kick in in stressful situations. But even then Dalu and Urshul are more important when on the hunt, Gauru is for that final fraction of a minute when your prey is cornered.<br /> <br /> For the Garou meanwhile Crinos is more important. Part of this is them being warriors and not hunters, and thus needing more consistent access to their most powerful form. As well as Garou Rage working differently, I'd personally probably have reworked it as Wrath if I'd been rebooting WtA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T06:29:45-07:00","id":1509173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509166#post1509166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbf the big limit on Gauru isn't the time limit (it's short, but CofD combat is fast and it is lore-wise meant to be only for killing), it's the fact that it doesn't let you act tactically. For the Uratha their wolf-man form is a tool, which fits with the fact that they're human/spirit hybrids, not human/wolf hybrids.<br /> <br /> Plus some can assume Gauru without the associated rage anyway, even if it does kick in in stressful situations. But even then Dalu and Urshul are more important when on the hunt, Gauru is for that final fraction of a minute when your prey is cornered.<br /> <br /> For the Garou meanwhile Crinos is more important. Part of this is them being warriors and not hunters, and thus needing more consistent access to their most powerful form. As well as Garou Rage working differently, I'd personally probably have reworked it as Wrath if I'd been rebooting WtA.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well said. Yeah the lack of tactical use is the main thing. Though, even pre-2nd ed. it was rare to see anyone use Gauru.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T06:49:19-07:00","id":1509174,"title":"","content":"The Get being booted out of Garou Nation really only makes sense from the standpoint of old old WtA lore ... which w5 isn't using. I really want to know if the Silver Fangs will have the 'constantly falling to Harno' problem that was talked about in older editions. So you have this 'its ok to be depressed but its not ok to have anger management issues' kind of dichotomy in what Garou Nation allows within it.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Garou Nation, wasn't there something that about how Garou Nation basically was dead and that it really was just a named that elders of a sept used to drum up support for themselves rather then a real united faction? So is that still a plot point or does Garou Nation actually have power and authority?<br /> <br /> Also my understanding is that the BSD still are a thing. I wonder if there is going to be a module that is going to have the party confronted with a pack of Get and they are going to be like 'You have to choose to fight with us against the BSD or become our enemies' like that is some kind of nail biting moral dilemma. Outstar even has emphasized that Garou are not good guys so what is it about the Get that make them so much worst that they where given the boot. Like there has to be an event where they just straight committed a purge of a sept for supposed corruption or something similar. I'm not sure if that was discussed in the &quot;Heart of the Forest&quot; VN or not.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T06:58:20-07:00","id":1509175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509174#post1509174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Get being booted out of Garou Nation really only makes sense from the standpoint of old old WtA lore ... which w5 isn't using.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fenrir being taken out, to me, is clearly an out of universe reason. People have complained about the glyph AND some arsehole players DID play them as nazi straight up.<br /> <br /> Paradox already has the Chechenya mess from the Camarilla book and the outrage at the V5 playtest ready-made characters, so they did not want to risk it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I really cannot see the Fenrir going before the Red Talons.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T07:20:30-07:00","id":1509176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509174#post1509174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Get being booted out of Garou Nation really only makes sense from the standpoint of old old WtA lore ... which w5 isn't using. I really want to know if the Silver Fangs will have the 'constantly falling to Harno' problem that was talked about in older editions. So you have this 'its ok to be depressed but its not ok to have anger management issues' kind of dichotomy in what Garou Nation allows within it.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Garou Nation, wasn't there something that about how Garou Nation basically was dead and that it really was just a named that elders of a sept used to drum up support for themselves rather then a real united faction? So is that still a plot point or does Garou Nation actually have power and authority?<br /> <br /> Also my understanding is that the BSD still are a thing. I wonder if there is going to be a module that is going to have the party confronted with a pack of Get and they are going to be like 'You have to choose to fight with us against the BSD or become our enemies' like that is some kind of nail biting moral dilemma. Outstar even has emphasized that Garou are not good guys so what is it about the Get that make them so much worst that they where given the boot. Like there has to be an event where they just straight committed a purge of a sept for supposed corruption or something similar. I'm not sure if that was discussed in the &quot;Heart of the Forest&quot; VN or not.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the introduction that we've seen still kinda doesn't address the issues I have with the new premise. There's the bit with the Get where I don't really see what makes them so extra bad.<br /> <br /> Then there's the bit on pg 10 where one paragraph ends with how the transition to being a Garou includes this awareness of how dire things are and so the paragraph ends with &quot;It's too late to avert the end.&quot; Next paragraph: &quot;That's no cause for fatalism, however. The Apocalypse may be upon them but that means every victory now becomes that much more important. Garou before them have failed Gaia but this generation of Garou still has purpose.&quot; That still doesn't quite address how the new generation of Garou is supposedly different from the old and how what you're doing is relevant in the context of the in-game world being absolutely doomed.<br /> <br /> As for the Garou-Nation, there's the entry in the Lexicon talking about it:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Garou-Nation: A loose coalition of Garou Tribes, ostensibly with common goals in service to Gaia; the Garou-Nation has sundered in the age of Apocalypse, and invoking it now can come acress as idealistic of backward-looking. </div> </div> </div>And there's a bit at the very beginning where it talks about how all Garou know things have gone wrong but they &quot;often disagree violently on how best to make the necessary changes.&quot; (where I'm again thinking &quot;Okay, so why are the Get so extra bad...?!&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T07:24:28-07:00","id":1509178,"title":"","content":"The Get have the misfortune of hitting on toxic masculinity, sexism, <i>and</i> fascism, which makes them really easy to strawman despite none of them applying to the Tribe as a whole. It's why Forsaken split their nobler aspects into the Blood Talons and their negative aspects into the Ivory Claws (who also got the worst of the Silver Fangs). Of course you can strawman any Tribe if you go far enough, I'm worried it's going to happen to the Glasswalkers now they follow Spider instead of Cockroach.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons meanwhile have their lupus-only nature making them less prevalent, along with the fact that 'anti-human' tendencies can be flipped into more 'pro-wolf' stuff without losing the core tribal identity.<br /> <br /> The Stargazers, honestly, come off as a bad relic of WW fetishizing Asia (specifically East Asia). They're the 'Asian Tribe', ludicrous when you compare the size of the continents, and they're werewolf Kung Fu monks. I can see removing them from the corebook just to spend more time and rework them in their entirety, especially as any rework of them is going to annoy someone. Yes, I know Revised solved a lot of these issues, but try explaining that so people with only a passing knowledge of Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T07:35:27-07:00","id":1509180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509178#post1509178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Get have the misfortune of hitting on toxic masculinity, sexism, <i>and</i> fascism, which makes them really easy to strawman despite none of them applying to the Tribe as a whole. It's why Forsaken split their nobler aspects into the Blood Talons and their negative aspects into the Ivory Claws (who also got the worst of the Silver Fangs). Of course you can strawman any Tribe if you go far enough, I'm worried it's going to happen to the Glasswalkers now they follow Spider instead of Cockroach.<br /> <br /> The Stargazers, honestly, come off as a bad relic of WW fetishizing Asia (specifically East Asia). They're the 'Asian Tribe', ludicrous when you compare the size of the continents, and they're werewolf Kung Fu monks. I can see removing them from the corebook just to spend more time and rework them in their entirety, especially as any rework of them is going to annoy someone. Yes, I know Revised solved a lot of these issues, but try explaining that so people with only a passing knowledge of Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, even if they've decided to turn the Get into an evil Tribe, at least I would like there to be a reason that feels less forced.<br /> <br /> And the Stargazers are in the book. They're in the Antagonist-section as an &quot;enigmatic ally&quot; NPC faction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Red Talons meanwhile have their lupus-only nature making them less prevalent, along with the fact that 'anti-human' tendencies can be flipped into more 'pro-wolf' stuff without losing the core tribal identity. </div> </div> </div>Now that you mention it there was another passage that caught my eye. On pg 10 it says: &quot;Part human, part wolf, but not wholly either, they are at once feared and even reviled by both wolves and humans.&quot; The idea that wolves fear and even revile Garou seems new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T07:40:29-07:00","id":1509181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509178#post1509178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Get have the misfortune of hitting on toxic masculinity, sexism, <i>and</i> fascism, which makes them really easy to strawman despite none of them applying to the Tribe as a whole. It's why Forsaken split their nobler aspects into the Blood Talons and their negative aspects into the Ivory Claws (who also got the worst of the Silver Fangs). Of course you can strawman any Tribe if you go far enough, I'm worried it's going to happen to the Glasswalkers now they follow Spider instead of Cockroach.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're retconning things left and right, though, why would any part of the Get remain as it was?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Red Talons meanwhile have their lupus-only nature making them less prevalent, along with the fact that 'anti-human' tendencies can be flipped into more 'pro-wolf' stuff without losing the core tribal identity. </div> </div> </div>No, I don't think it's going to be that easy. Being pro-wolf means pushing back hard against a lot of humanity's interests. It means going against the human moral community in lots of big ways. It means that there will be blood, even if we've shed the edgelord stuff about Yuletide Rites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Stargazers, honestly, come off as a bad relic of WW fetishizing Asia (specifically East Asia). They're the 'Asian Tribe', ludicrous when you compare the size of the continents, and they're werewolf Kung Fu monks. I can see removing them from the corebook just to spend more time and rework them in their entirety, especially as any rework of them is going to annoy someone. Yes, I know Revised solved a lot of these issues, but try explaining that so people with only a passing knowledge of Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>Even weirder was how they were supposed to be smaller in number than the Red Talons but obviously weren't, especially not when connected to Asia, aka the continent on Earth with <i>the most</i> humans on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T07:44:44-07:00","id":1509182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509180#post1509180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that you mention it there was another passage that caught my eye. On pg 10 it says: &quot;Part human, part wolf, but not wholly either, they are at once feared and even reviled by both wolves and humans.&quot; The idea that wolves fear and even revile Garou seems new.</div> </div> </div> </div>There have actually been bits going back to 1e where some lupus characters were ostracized by their birth back and driven out. It wasn't as typical as homids being ostracized, though, which seemed like every other character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T07:45:08-07:00","id":1509183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509176#post1509176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the introduction that we've seen still kinda doesn't address the issues I have with the new premise. There's the bit with the Get where I don't really see what makes them so extra bad.<br /> <br /> Then there's the bit on pg 10 where one paragraph ends with how the transition to being a Garou includes this awareness of how dire things are and so the paragraph ends with &quot;It's too late to avert the end.&quot; Next paragraph: &quot;That's no cause for fatalism, however. The Apocalypse may be upon them but that means every victory now becomes that much more important. Garou before them have failed Gaia but this generation of Garou still has purpose.&quot; That still doesn't quite address how the new generation of Garou is supposedly different from the old and how what you're doing is relevant in the context of the in-game world being absolutely doomed.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this comes to the point of if <b>every victory</b> is so important that even small victories are something to be celebrated, what are the Get doing or did that makes it so they have no victories. I feel like again we are just going to have this Mystery Box that we are supposed to be ooh and aah at like 'what could it possibly be?' but all it does is make the setting itself feel uncomplete and loses its verisimilitude. Which for RPG nerds, like myself, is really important for enjoyment and getting into the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509176#post1509176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Garou-Nation, there's the entry in the Lexicon talking about it:<br /> &quot;Garou-Nation: A loose coalition of Garou Tribes, ostensibly with common goals in service to Gaia; the Garou-Nation has sundered in the age of Apocalypse, and invoking it now can come acress as idealistic of backward-looking.&quot;<br /> <br /> And there's a bit at the very beginning where it talks about how all Garou know things have gone wrong but they &quot;often disagree violently on how best to make the necessary changes.&quot; (where I'm again thinking &quot;Okay, so why are the Get so extra bad...?!&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>This just makes it even less sensical because If A) the Garou-Nation has sundered in the age of Apocalypse and B) invoking it now can come across as idealistic of backward-looking, then <b>who</b> kicked the Get out and why, if the answer is 'Garou-Nation', then why should anyone care since Garou-Nation is a defuncted entity that seemingly no one cares about. If it's not 'Garou-Nation' then why isn't this other power talked about at all because it seems like they have some pull with the entire Garou people and can organize them in some way.<br /> <br /> What is it about the Get that every independent Sept has come together in agreement that 'We don't traffic with Get.'\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T07:46:51-07:00","id":1509184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509180#post1509180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that you mention it there was another passage that caught my eye. On pg 10 it says: &quot;Part human, part wolf, but not wholly either, they are at once feared and even reviled by both wolves and humans.&quot; The idea that wolves fear and even revile Garou seems new.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not new, it is just rarely used because most games do not focus on wolf kin as 'people.' Essentially, Rage scares regular wolves as much as regular humans. So Red Talons are no more at peace with regular wolves than Glass Walkers are with regular humans. This is often ignored to make the Talons seem more at peace with their wolf-kin, though.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T07:56:13-07:00","id":1509185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509086#post1509086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tone from back in October when Justin Achilli was talking about this was certainly very different compared to how Outstar talked about it now. The word &quot;action&quot; in the sense of &quot;doing something about the situation you're in&quot; came up a lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> The first name was definitely Christopher but I'm not sure about the surname. Once the book comes out the credits-page will certainly help.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The name is Christopher Gunning. He is the owner of Weaponized Ink and has a fairly long history in the TTRPG industry.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, that is not <i>my</i> name. I just work with him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":1813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","user":"grimjaws","date":". 04-21-2023, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T08:12:08-07:00","id":1509189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509185#post1509185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The name is Christopher Gunning. He is the owner of Weaponized Ink and has a fairly long history in the TTRPG industry.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, that is not <i>my</i> name. I just work with him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! I knew someone from WI was working on it but couldn't find anyone from there in the list of freelancers that the Developer released. That makes sense now.<br /> <br /> Well, at least we know the intro adventure will be decent even if he had to make a silk purse out of a sows ear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T08:21:20-07:00","id":1509191,"title":"","content":"Its probably worth noting that the groundwork for soft retconning the nazi out of the get goes as far back as revised at least just focus on that characterisation and loose the Tribe symbol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T09:04:02-07:00","id":1509196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509191#post1509191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its probably worth noting that the groundwork for soft retconning the nazi out of the get goes as far back as revised at least just focus on that characterisation and loose the Tribe symbol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, that is why it is such a baffling thing. I fully believe Paradox got gunshy after the two aforementioned messes.<br /> <br /> Why I feel Red Talons should have gone instead of Fenrir, is the years upon years the tribe has been used as NPCs. Red Talon PCs are about as rare as Stargazer PCs in some circles if not rarer. And as much as I enjoy the tribe, it really IS one that suits a bunch of garou going nuts with Rage the best. Since Talon culture is about denying ANY human thought or behaviour as unclean yet still being human in their tribe structure and the whole denial business, them deciding to just go ham makes perfect sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T10:20:36-07:00","id":1509211,"title":"","content":"But, once again, all the ideas of the Nazi Get only exist in WtA and shouldn't be a part of W5 since it has its own lore and timeline. The Devs had every opportunity to make every tribe into whatever they wanted to such a degree of changing names, symbols, and totem. <br /> <br /> The only reason, that I can see at this point, to make the Get the enemy is to try to sell a perception of what the game and to a larger extend what the company stands for rather then any logical reason why one tribe is booted. Which doesn't help clear up the picture being painted by what this means for the Garou in particular and the setting at large. It hard to approach the game on it's own merits when the basic core has holes in it that cause players to fall into. If key events of the setting have no answer then the setting falls apart. You can say that the entire Get tribe fell into hauglosk but that only brings up other things like 'How was that confrimed, what did they do to make people believe that, was there some event that was undeniable proof.'<br /> <br /> Speaking to that as well, if we are to believe that the entire Get tribe has fallen into hauglosk, this state that you are so filled with rage that you lose yourself and just want to murder. How are the Get even a tribe that is still around? Wouldn't they all have been killed due to not able to do anything else besides kill? How do they get more of their Tribe, its not like they have they have people looking for lost cubs to induct into their Tribe. Do they even able to think clearly to talk to any spirit let alone their totem spirit? And if it's not some authority that has banned the Get from Garou-Nation and instead they left on their own to fight their own way because they didn't care for whatever Garou-Nation was doing, then how are they 'fallen' and what evidence is there they are in hauglosk?<br /> <br /> At this point I just don't have enough information to answer any of these questions and getting the book to see if these questions get answered seems like a waste of money.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T10:41:26-07:00","id":1509214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509211#post1509211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only reason, that I can see at this point, to make the Get the enemy is to try to sell a perception of what the game and to a larger extend what the company stands for rather then any logical reason why one tribe is booted.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much it, I think. This, combined with the past controversies and some of the more vocal fans railing against the tribe.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T12:05:52-07:00","id":1509223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509185#post1509185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The name is Christopher Gunning. He is the owner of Weaponized Ink and has a fairly long history in the TTRPG industry.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, that is not <i>my</i> name. I just work with him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for correcting that. I look forward to reading what his introductory adventure will be like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509182#post1509182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There have actually been bits going back to 1e where some lupus characters were ostracized by their birth back and driven out. It wasn't as typical as homids being ostracized, though, which seemed like every other character.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509184#post1509184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not new, it is just rarely used because most games do not focus on wolf kin as 'people.' Essentially, Rage scares regular wolves as much as regular humans. So Red Talons are no more at peace with regular wolves than Glass Walkers are with regular humans. This is often ignored to make the Talons seem more at peace with their wolf-kin, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay, thanks for clarifying that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509211#post1509211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, once again, all the ideas of the Nazi Get only exist in WtA and shouldn't be a part of W5 since it has its own lore and timeline. The Devs had every opportunity to make every tribe into whatever they wanted to such a degree of changing names, symbols, and totem.<br /> <br /> The only reason, that I can see at this point, to make the Get the enemy is to try to sell a perception of what the game and to a larger extend what the company stands for rather then any logical reason why one tribe is booted. Which doesn't help clear up the picture being painted by what this means for the Garou in particular and the setting at large. It hard to approach the game on it's own merits when the basic core has holes in it that cause players to fall into. If key events of the setting have no answer then the setting falls apart. You can say that the entire Get tribe fell into hauglosk but that only brings up other things like 'How was that confrimed, what did they do to make people believe that, was there some event that was undeniable proof.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Another option I could think of is that the Get are something similar to the Vigilante-hunter-orgs in H5. Those were &quot;hunter-orgs&quot; who essentially are just hunter-cells but similar to other hunter-orgs they also have an ulterior motive and the Vigilante-hunter-org's is... <i>only </i>caring about killing supernatural entities. Where the other hunter-org fit the design-goal of being dark reflections of the Creeds, the Vigilantes are identical to the hunter-cell-PC-groups - except<i> they're doing it wrong</i> (I think the problem it's trying to point at is that these hunters don't have Touchstones). And I could picture Get filling a similar role as an NPC-faction who are nearly identical to the PC-groups but <i>they're doing it wrong</i> and that's why you're supposed to oppose them.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE=MrNatas;n1509211Speaking to that as well, if we are to believe that the entire Get tribe has fallen into hauglosk, this state that you are so filled with rage that you lose yourself and just want to murder. How are the Get even a tribe that is still around? Wouldn't they all have been killed due to not able to do anything else besides kill? How do they get more of their Tribe, its not like they have they have people looking for lost cubs to induct into their Tribe. Do they even able to think clearly to talk to any spirit let alone their totem spirit? And if it's not some authority that has banned the Get from Garou-Nation and instead they left on their own to fight their own way because they didn't care for whatever Garou-Nation was doing, then how are they 'fallen' and what evidence is there they are in hauglosk?[/QUOTE]<br /> Now that we know that every Garou in W5 can suffer from Hauglosk, that's an important question: How exactly are Get capable of being in permanent Hauglosk? And how can Get even operate under this condition? The only way I could imagine this happening is if their Patron Spirit is enforcing this since that would be the lowest common denominator for Get-Garou around the globe... but that would raise a whole bunch of other questions immediately, I guess.<br /> <br /> As for looking for new recruits, it actually gets mentioned that your PC-packs potentially are competing with Get-packs in recruiting Kin. They're indirectly mentioned on pg 11 under the &quot;What do Werewolves do&quot;-section where under the point &quot;looking out for other of their kind&quot; they're mentioning how important is to keep these Kin away from the clutches of the &quot;so-called fallen Tribes&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T12:49:47-07:00","id":1509226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509223#post1509223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option I could think of is that the Get are something similar to the Vigilante-hunter-orgs in H5. Those were &quot;hunter-orgs&quot; who essentially are just hunter-cells but similar to other hunter-orgs they also have an ulterior motive and the Vigilante-hunter-org's is... <i>only </i>caring about killing supernatural entities. Where the other hunter-org fit the design-goal of being dark reflections of the Creeds, the Vigilantes are identical to the hunter-cell-PC-groups - except<i> they're doing it wrong</i> (I think the problem it's trying to point at is that these hunters don't have Touchstones). And I could picture Get filling a similar role as an NPC-faction who are nearly identical to the PC-groups but <i>they're doing it wrong</i> and that's why you're supposed to oppose them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet it seems like doing it wrong is some how more inline with what they are supposed to be doing. It's so frustration that we have a 'no true Scotsmen' as a metaphysical thing that separates the 'proper' Garou from the 'improper' Garou if this is the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509223#post1509223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that we know that every Garou in W5 can suffer from Hauglosk, that's an important question: How exactly are Get capable of being in permanent Hauglosk? And how can Get even operate under this condition? The only way I could imagine this happening is if their Patron Spirit is enforcing this since that would be the lowest common denominator for Get-Garou around the globe... but that would raise a whole bunch of other questions immediately, I guess.<br /> <br /> As for looking for new recruits, it actually gets mentioned that your PC-packs potentially are competing with Get-packs in recruiting Kin. They're indirectly mentioned on pg 11 under the &quot;What do Werewolves do&quot;-section where under the point &quot;looking out for other of their kind&quot; they're mentioning how important is to keep these Kin away from the clutches of the &quot;so-called fallen Tribes&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>But how are the Get-packs able to recruit Kin if they are in Hauglosk? Like is the Get's Hauglosk condition somehow different that they are able to think, track, talk, and preform rituals? This isn't like the BSD where they can just throw a Garou into a pit and they become Wyrm-y. At this point I'm more convinced that Hauglosk is more like Wassail and it makes werewolves into Wights. They can still do whatever they just have the 'wolf' in control and given up all 'human.' Which just means that all the more reason why the <b>Red Talons</b> fit that idea better.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T02:54:24-07:00","id":1509264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509223#post1509223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another option I could think of is that the Get are something similar to the Vigilante-hunter-orgs in H5. Those were &quot;hunter-orgs&quot; who essentially are just hunter-cells but similar to other hunter-orgs they also have an ulterior motive and the Vigilante-hunter-org's is... <i>only </i>caring about killing supernatural entities. Where the other hunter-org fit the design-goal of being dark reflections of the Creeds, the Vigilantes are identical to the hunter-cell-PC-groups - except<i> they're doing it wrong</i> (I think the problem it's trying to point at is that these hunters don't have Touchstones). And I could picture Get filling a similar role as an NPC-faction who are nearly identical to the PC-groups but <i>they're doing it wrong</i> and that's why you're supposed to oppose them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>see the trouble with that is it sounds awesome and something you'd want to play especially if you staple a lot of norse stuff. Which goes against the 5th ed aesthetic of being ineffective and focused on the 'street'.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T06:22:01-07:00","id":1509269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509264#post1509264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> see the trouble with that is it sounds awesome and something you'd want to play especially if you staple a lot of norse stuff. Which goes against the 5th ed aesthetic of being ineffective and focused on the 'street'.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You also wouldn't be stapling on Norse stuff unless it was some declaration of how you're going to fucking kill the Aesir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T06:55:18-07:00","id":1509272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509226#post1509226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how are the Get-packs able to recruit Kin if they are in Hauglosk?</div> </div> </div> </div>This part, of course, only gets even weirder because of how the process of joining a Tribe, being a Kin and having your First Change are all stuff Garou don't understand (and just like the Umbra are also treateded mysteries). And the section &quot;seeking out others of your kind&quot; talks about recruiting Kin and guiding/mentoring them to become a Garou and join a Tribe or accept a particular Patron-Spirit but because of how it's set up in the W5-setting this isn't the only way to do that. You see that with the in-character-perspective from the previous page where you have a guy who had undergone his First Change but there's no talk of other Garou finding him to explain it all. Instead, there it's described as this process of self-realization that guides him to becoming a Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509264#post1509264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">see the trouble with that is it sounds awesome and something you'd want to play especially if you staple a lot of norse stuff. Which goes against the 5th ed aesthetic of being ineffective and focused on the 'street'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like instead of the tagline being &quot;When will you Rage?&quot;, it's something like &quot;Become Rage. Seek vengeance. Die well.&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T07:08:04-07:00","id":1509273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509269#post1509269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You also wouldn't be stapling on Norse stuff unless it was some declaration of how you're going to fucking kill the Aesir.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Scion 1e and W20 are probably cross compatible.<br /> <br /> I think the idea is meant to be that the Get are rampaging everywhere and causing too much collateral damage, but considering that the Garou apparently can't tell what is and isn't of the Wyrm anymore who knows if it's actually more. Meanwhile real Garou are hunkering down, defending their Caern, and killing the occasional lobbyist, but only on Tuesday and Thursday evenings as they've got to go to the office and spend time with the kids.<br /> <br /> Basically the game might very well be designed to appeal to middle-class 20-30 year olds who think the planet is on fire but are also annoyed that Extinction Rebellion have blocked their commute. Do something to change the world but not too much, then you might inconvenience someone <br /> <br /> I just hope the Resources background got changed from the 1/session boost. Because if I'm going to have to spend six weeks verifying that the council secretary who authorised a new landfill site is actually a fomori I really should be able to wear a different style every scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T13:21:41-07:00","id":1509309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509273#post1509273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, Scion 1e and W20 are probably cross compatible.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>[Abridged Future Gohan] In what regard? [/]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T03:21:59-07:00","id":1509358,"title":"","content":"I've said it before and I'll say it again - W20 presents two really good candidate tribes who are canonically near the edge of a serious fall: The Red Talons and Silver Fangs. For pretty much every other tribe there is an extremist faction who have been destroyed (Cyberdogs, the few Get who went Nazi) or pushed into the sidelines to bitterly stew about stuff (Mother's Fundamentalists, the CoG who want to kill all animals to create a permanent peace). With the Red Talons and Silver Fangs, you could argue that the bad part of the Tribe just *is* the Tribe, with the more helpful aspect instead being in the minority; for instance the silver fangs who push for reform.<br /> <br /> If I'd written W5 and I'd been told &quot;we need a hook&quot;, then a significant portion of Red Talons starting to fight the rest of the Garou Nation for 'betraying wolves', having made a bargain with a powerful wolf spirit to help the species survive at any cost, would be up there. Alongside this there would be greater emphasis on the crisis of identity within the Silver Fangs and how they are growing increasingly alienated from the rest of the nation, with more falling to Harano, joining the BSDs or getting killed in duels or assassinations with each passing year.<br /> <br /> And even then you'd have the option to play a heroic Silver Fang or Red Talon who understands what the Tribe is really about, what it was meant to do for Gaia, and has hope that they can salvage something worthwhile out of the chaos by rallying a few good Garou they find along the path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T05:19:45-07:00","id":1509364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509358#post1509358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said it before and I'll say it again - W20 presents two really good candidate tribes who are canonically near the edge of a serious fall: The Red Talons and Silver Fangs. For pretty much every other tribe there is an extremist faction who have been destroyed (Cyberdogs, the few Get who went Nazi) or pushed into the sidelines to bitterly stew about stuff (Mother's Fundamentalists, the CoG who want to kill all animals to create a permanent peace). With the Red Talons and Silver Fangs, you could argue that the bad part of the Tribe just *is* the Tribe, with the more helpful aspect instead being in the minority; for instance the silver fangs who push for reform.<br /> <br /> If I'd written W5 and I'd been told &quot;we need a hook&quot;, then a significant portion of Red Talons starting to fight the rest of the Garou Nation for 'betraying wolves', having made a bargain with a powerful wolf spirit to help the species survive at any cost, would be up there. Alongside this there would be greater emphasis on the crisis of identity within the Silver Fangs and how they are growing increasingly alienated from the rest of the nation, with more falling to Harano, joining the BSDs or getting killed in duels or assassinations with each passing year.<br /> <br /> And even then you'd have the option to play a heroic Silver Fang or Red Talon who understands what the Tribe is really about, what it was meant to do for Gaia, and has hope that they can salvage something worthwhile out of the chaos by rallying a few good Garou they find along the path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Silver Fangs also make a good candidate because of how the Garou Nation has fallen in the W5 setting. Seeing themselves as leaders of the Garou Nation, its fall should have some serious consequences for the Tribe and what they think of themselves as well as what others think of them.<br /> <br /> Even aside from that, it makes me wonder how they're gonna portray the Silver Fangs in the corebook. They claimed to be the leaders of the Garou Nation and since it has fallen and so much has already been lost, you gotta wonder why anybody would even take any Silver Fangs' desire to be a leader seriously at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T08:35:03-07:00","id":1509379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509358#post1509358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Red Talons and Silver Fangs, you could argue that the bad part of the Tribe just *is* the Tribe, with the more helpful aspect instead being in the minority; for instance the silver fangs who push for reform.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, with the Talons that is not true. Talons have their own hated camp; the Dying Cubs. The Dying Cubs intentionally torture humans for days at a time to 'feed' the earth with their pain. Regular Red Talons kill humans, yes, but they kill them quickly like any other prey.<br /> <br /> But the Fangs? No, they do not really have that. Gray Raptors maybe, but even then they are MOSTLY quietly accepted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509364#post1509364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Silver Fangs also make a good candidate because of how the Garou Nation has fallen in the W5 setting. Seeing themselves as leaders of the Garou Nation, its fall should have some serious consequences for the Tribe and what they think of themselves as well as what others think of them.<br /> <br /> Even aside from that, it makes me wonder how they're gonna portray the Silver Fangs in the corebook. They claimed to be the leaders of the Garou Nation and since it has fallen and so much has already been lost, you gotta wonder why anybody would even take any Silver Fangs' desire to be a leader seriously at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, there are many reasons why I'd swap the Fenrir and Fangs too. First of all, Fangs ACTUALLY require blood purity, unlike the Fenrir. You cannot play a Fang with 0 pure breed.<br /> <br /> Second, as stated above, Fangs have done the least work to actually fix things. While Alby is trying his best, the fact is there are many Fangs who do not see any reason to make amends.<br /> <br /> This is why the Fenrir as the Haglust fallen tribe seems entirely made due to out of universe reasons.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T12:05:04-07:00","id":1509402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509379#post1509379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, there are many reasons why I'd swap the Fenrir and Fangs too. First of all, Fangs ACTUALLY require blood purity, unlike the Fenrir. You cannot play a Fang with 0 pure breed.<br /> <br /> Second, as stated above, Fangs have done the least work to actually fix things. While Alby is trying his best, the fact is there are many Fangs who do not see any reason to make amends.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Even beginning with the basics... In a setting with the Garou/Kin-dynamic where Purebreed doesn't exist - what is the Silver Fangs' original claim to leadership based on in the W5 setting...?<br /> <br /> Then again, even more generally: Because of how much the W5 previews (and the shown introduction) focus on how the Garou-Nation has fallen apart and how the Tribes haven't been working together, I'm wondering how the Garou-Nation ever existed in the first place... With old editions, the dysfunctional state of the Garou-Nation is a point of crisis but in an apocalyptic setting complaining about the Garou-Nation feels like a &quot;No shit, now what...?&quot;-scenario.<br /> <br /> And somehow this new version of the Silver Fangs has to find a place in all of this. Even if they believe it themselves, wouldn't any attempt for them to try to convince other Garou to make them leaders again or insist the Garou-Nation can be revived somehow just turn them into a bunch of con-artists...?<br /> <br /> The version that has fallen to the Wyrm could be all about Silver Fangs being these evangelistic, super-idealistic, optimistic Garou who are trying to scam other Garou into putting them right back into top-positions. But where it used to be the good of the Garou-Nation, now it's all about personality-cults. Like, the mantra is &quot;The Tribe has failed - but <i>I</i> haven't.&quot; If you know Warhammer, I'm thinking of the kind of vainglorious excess you'd associate with a Slaanesh-follower.<br /> <br /> Writing this also made me think of another idea. Instead of the Get falling and becoming a fallen Tribe, how about a scenario where the Garou-Nation has fallen, it has become certain the Apocalypse is nigh and in these dark times any Garou might give in to self-/destructive urges. Instead of having just that one Tribe becoming bad guys suddenly, Garou in general are in a moment of deep crisis and getting stuck in permanent Hauglosk, for example, is something that happens to individuals, not entire Tribes.<br /> <br /> Then again, one of the things that I personally don't like is that in this W5-setup aside from the Garou-Nation being torn apart nothing else feels like a game that is mid-Apocalypse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T13:41:27-07:00","id":1509408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509402#post1509402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even beginning with the basics... In a setting with the Garou/Kin-dynamic where Purebreed doesn't exist - what is the Silver Fangs' original claim to leadership based on in the W5 setting...?<br /> <br /> Then again, even more generally: Because of how much the W5 previews (and the shown introduction) focus on how the Garou-Nation has fallen apart and how the Tribes haven't been working together, I'm wondering how the Garou-Nation ever existed in the first place... With old editions, the dysfunctional state of the Garou-Nation is a point of crisis but in an apocalyptic setting complaining about the Garou-Nation feels like a &quot;No shit, now what...?&quot;-scenario.<br /> <br /> And somehow this new version of the Silver Fangs has to find a place in all of this. Even if they believe it themselves, wouldn't any attempt for them to try to convince other Garou to make them leaders again or insist the Garou-Nation can be revived somehow just turn them into a bunch of con-artists...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I frankly think the Fangs will be like this in W5; Garou who are obsessed with nobility, leadership, knighthood and such. They have no actual pure breed or anything like that, instead, their nobility comes from their human side AND from their historical deeds. Their fatal flaw is that they take the concept of knighthood a bit too seriously, not that they are the definition of garou who refuse to accept they fucked up.<br /> <br /> I mean, here are two sources that hint at this;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/GzZdoyZ.png\" target=\"_blank\">Retaliation tribe cards</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://s3-eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/pdx-campaign-wp-data/uploads/sites/10/2022/10/03105504/werewolf_tribes-576x1024.png\" target=\"_blank\">Official Site tribe verbs.</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T13:43:56-07:00","id":1509409,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> you're touching on something I really resonate with - changes like falling happen to individuals and groups. A Tribe can fall, yes, but it isn't 100% of members. Anything that claims 100% of anything was converted, wiped out etc. is likely misleading or poorly thought out.<br /> <br /> A crisis across all Garou is far more interesting. Have each tribe be in a moment of crisis where they have a villainous movement (if you want to make it easy to explain and market) who are pushing for some really awful response to the crisis, and a reconciliatory movement who emphasize the best quality of the Tribe. Each Tribe is in a state where it is in conflict between its best and worst aspects.<br /> <br /> This is, in truth, just Camps. Intra-tribe conflicts are the reason &quot;Nazi Get&quot; and &quot;Kill Literally All Conscious Beings CoG&quot; and &quot;Turn Wolves into Cyborgs Glass Walkers&quot; and &quot;Murder Rival Kinfolk and Restart Impergium Fianna&quot; existed. A Chronicle based around a specific Tribe needed a villain! But then dumb memes based on a game of telephone involving maybe 1 person who has actually played WTA happen, and you wind up with people thinking &quot;the Get are Nazis&quot; or whatever. Of all the WoD games, Werewolf seems to be the most willfully and consistently misunderstood for some reason.<br /> <br /> Anyways all this to say that if your new lore tells me that 100% of Get of Fenris members have fallen into a certain state, and you don't show me renegades who are still staying true or have fled to other tribes etc. then you're selling me a setting which doesn't pass the &quot;okay but let's think about this for 2 seconds&quot; test. So hopefully W5 will give it more thought than that - we'll have to wait and see!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T19:29:01-07:00","id":1509429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509408#post1509408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean, here are two sources that hint at this;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/GzZdoyZ.png\" target=\"_blank\">Retaliation tribe cards</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://s3-eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/pdx-campaign-wp-data/uploads/sites/10/2022/10/03105504/werewolf_tribes-576x1024.png\" target=\"_blank\">Official Site tribe verbs.</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind the makers of Retaliation said they had to cobble those together from previous WtA editions and their own imagination because Paradox gave them bugger all info and what they did get was mainly from the Hunters Entertainment version of W5.<br /> <br /> Just realised that 3 out of 4 of the Coggie's verbs are essentially synonyms....most of which are more Stargazeresque anyway....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T22:31:52-07:00","id":1509447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509429#post1509429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bear in mind the makers of Retaliation said they had to cobble those together from previous WtA editions and their own imagination because Paradox gave them bugger all info and what they did get was mainly from the Hunters Entertainment version of W5.<br /> <br /> Just realised that 3 out of 4 of the Coggie's verbs are essentially synonyms....most of which are more Stargazeresque anyway....</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not know that, thank you for informing me.<br /> <br /> Well, then the tribe previews are even more important, since we basically only have (maybe inaccurate) verbs of the tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T02:55:21-07:00","id":1509462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509429#post1509429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bear in mind the makers of Retaliation said they had to cobble those together from previous WtA editions and their own imagination because Paradox gave them bugger all info and what they did get was mainly from the Hunters Entertainment version of W5.<br /> <br /> Just realised that 3 out of 4 of the Coggie's verbs are essentially synonyms....most of which are more Stargazeresque anyway....</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to that: The reason Retaliation didn't get a lot of info on the version of W5 which will come out this year was because that version of W5 was still deep in development. But because of the board-game-developer's production-schedule and their limited funds they couldn't just wait for the WOD-team to finish the writing at least (and we know that it took them until January of this year).<br /> <br /> They were talking to the WOD-team, though, and they got some info from them. Like, for example, what they added to the boardgame was the W5-bit that Garou can't use weapons in Crinos-form (like Klaives).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T14:27:06-07:00","id":1509522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509409#post1509409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> you're touching on something I really resonate with - changes like falling happen to individuals and groups. A Tribe can fall, yes, but it isn't 100% of members. Anything that claims 100% of anything was converted, wiped out etc. is likely misleading or poorly thought out.<br /> <br /> A crisis across all Garou is far more interesting. Have each tribe be in a moment of crisis where they have a villainous movement (if you want to make it easy to explain and market) who are pushing for some really awful response to the crisis, and a reconciliatory movement who emphasize the best quality of the Tribe. Each Tribe is in a state where it is in conflict between its best and worst aspects.<br /> <br /> This is, in truth, just Camps. Intra-tribe conflicts are the reason &quot;Nazi Get&quot; and &quot;Kill Literally All Conscious Beings CoG&quot; and &quot;Turn Wolves into Cyborgs Glass Walkers&quot; and &quot;Murder Rival Kinfolk and Restart Impergium Fianna&quot; existed. A Chronicle based around a specific Tribe needed a villain! But then dumb memes based on a game of telephone involving maybe 1 person who has actually played WTA happen, and you wind up with people thinking &quot;the Get are Nazis&quot; or whatever. Of all the WoD games, Werewolf seems to be the most willfully and consistently misunderstood for some reason.<br /> <br /> Anyways all this to say that if your new lore tells me that 100% of Get of Fenris members have fallen into a certain state, and you don't show me renegades who are still staying true or have fled to other tribes etc. then you're selling me a setting which doesn't pass the &quot;okay but let's think about this for 2 seconds&quot; test. So hopefully W5 will give it more thought than that - we'll have to wait and see!</div> </div> </div> </div>The other great thing about this is that the Get can look at the Nazis in their midst (and so on for the other tribes), say, &quot;We're not with that guy,&quot; and you have a genuine, in-universe reason for people to clean house and reject the extremists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T08:56:27-07:00","id":1509732,"title":"","content":"The Renegade-store-page for the W5-corebook has a preview for the Glasswalkers up. I guess, that means it's because people voted for them to be the first preview.<br /> <br /> First impressions from me:<ul><li>Very sparse on history and culture of the Tribe (the Garou-Nation falling apart isn't even addressed, for example)</li> <li>It starts by trying to link example scenarios to the whole verbs-thing and I gotta say &quot;repurpose a sequence of blast doors to trap a gang of formori&quot; reminds me of a sci-fi-space-ship-thing and not urban fantasy present-day-stuff. Multiple blast-doors...? What kind of Caern is that...?</li> <li>&quot;Who are the Glass-Walkers?&quot; starts with talking about the Tribe's close relationship with tools and therefore a close connection to humans. Then it mentions that present-day Garou are rankled by past Garou being on the wrong side in the Impergium. Okay... so why were they on the wrong side...?</li> <li>Favor: Extra die to building and repairing things. Same issue as with Entrepreneurial Creed in H5: A repair/creation-system was basically non-existent in H5 and I guess, we'll see how W5 handles it. But an extra die to actions that are 100% up to STs anyway feels a bit weak...</li> <li>Ban: Only recover one Willpower next session if complex machinery gets destroyed. It's weird that it's Willpower-recovery because that feels more like a personal thing unrelated to stuff like a Patron-Spirit.</li> <li>In regards to Archetypes... The Urban-Planner sounds like the perfect setup for the idea that being a Garou is something you do in your freetime while mainly being busy with some kind of 9-to-5-job.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T09:20:19-07:00","id":1509735,"title":"","content":"I am so far happy with Glass Walkers, thit concept is similar as in other editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T10:35:52-07:00","id":1509745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509732#post1509732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Who are the Glass-Walkers?&quot; starts with talking about the Tribe's close relationship with tools and therefore a close connection to humans. Then it mentions that present-day Garou are rankled by past Garou being on the wrong side in the Impergium. Okay... so why were they on the wrong side...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to know what side was the &quot;wrong side&quot; because that would say a lot about the Garou's outlook in general and the Tribe in specific. Did they side with the human and do they feel like even if the Impergium was wrong them siding with humans made Garou-Nation weaker? Did they side with Garou to kill humans and feel like that has cause the Human-Garou relationship to sour and thus put them on the path of destruction? Some more here would be good to give the Tribe character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509732#post1509732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Favor: Extra die to building and repairing things. Same issue as with Entrepreneurial Creed in H5: A repair/creation-system was basically non-existent in H5 and I guess, we'll see how W5 handles it. But an extra die to actions that are 100% up to STs anyway feels a bit weak...</div> </div> </div> </div>Build and repair are actions that are always so few that even if we get really good creation rules it's not going to be as useful to something like 'Silver Fangs get an extra dice when persuading people.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509732#post1509732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ban: Only recover one Willpower next session if complex machinery gets destroyed. It's weird that it's Willpower-recovery because that feels more like a personal thing unrelated to stuff like a Patron-Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm not understanding because of how this is written but, is it saying that GlassWalkers recover willpower if a complex machine gets destroyed or if they keep a complex machine safe they can recover more then one Willpower next session? I will admit this an ignorance of how willpower recovery works in WoD5.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T10:45:49-07:00","id":1509746,"title":"","content":"Considering lupus is no longer a statted thing, I find it interesting how the preview STILL takes time to say GWs don't have many of them.<br /> <br /> To the other stuff; As Knightingale above said, the example characters seem very much like 'doing a hobby in-between jobs.' Also, given how W5 sounds like, the emphasis on GWs choosing to side with humans sounds a bit weird.<br /> <br /> All in all, I find this preview a bit too surface level and non-indicative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T10:47:37-07:00","id":1509747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509745#post1509745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm not understanding because of how this is written but, is it saying that GlassWalkers recover willpower if a complex machine gets destroyed or if they keep a complex machine safe they can recover more then one Willpower next session? I will admit this an ignorance of how willpower recovery works in WoD5.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It means that if a complex machine gets destroyed, the GW recovers only ONE wp between sessions.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T10:48:11-07:00","id":1509748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509745#post1509745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd like to know what side was the &quot;wrong side&quot; because that would say a lot about the Garou's outlook in general and the Tribe in specific. Did they side with the human and do they feel like even if the Impergium was wrong them siding with humans made Garou-Nation weaker? Did they side with Garou to kill humans and feel like that has cause the Human-Garou relationship to sour and thus put them on the path of destruction? Some more here would be good to give the Tribe character.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It says the GW sided with the Garou against the humans during the Impergium and that is what rankles present-day GW who are much more pro-human... and that's it. The Tribe-section doesn't say anything more about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509745#post1509745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Build and repair are actions that are always so few that even if we get really good creation rules it's not going to be as useful to something like 'Silver Fangs get an extra dice when persuading people.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why I compared it to that H5-Creed. How useful is that really if you don't have a good system that illustrates the benefits of engaging in that action? The way it's right now, it's pretty much all ST-fiat anyway so why bother with dice-bonuses...?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509745#post1509745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm not understanding because of how this is written but, is it saying that GlassWalkers recover willpower if a complex machine gets destroyed or if they keep a complex machine safe they can recover more then one Willpower next session? I will admit this an ignorance of how willpower recovery works in WoD5.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it says if the Garou destroys a complex machine Willpower-recovery for the next session will be kept at one Willpower.<br /> <br /> Now that I thought about it... this also makes me wonder with something like this: What if a bad roll with Rage-Dice leads to your character losing control and doing something like destroying complex machinery...? Does that count? I wonder if they address that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T11:04:30-07:00","id":1509749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509747#post1509747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It means that if a complex machine gets destroyed, the GW recovers only ONE wp between sessions.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509748#post1509748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it says if the Garou destroys a complex machine Willpower-recovery for the next session will be kept at one Willpower.<br /> <br /> Now that I thought about it... this also makes me wonder with something like this: What if a bad roll with Rage-Dice leads to your character losing control and doing something like destroying complex machinery...? Does that count? I wonder if they address that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification. I would think that it would be even on accident, rather it's rage rolls or a botch on test.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T11:22:38-07:00","id":1509751,"title":"","content":"The Car Liberator really bothers me for multiple reasons.<br /> <br /> For one &quot;Maybe there's a bit of ethical gymnastics to justify the enterprise&quot; seems to imply that NORMALLY Glass Walkers do not break the law or that they'd care about the morality of human law.<br /> <br /> Second, for a concept about a werewolf of the city, seems way too small time and simple to serve as a character concept. Outside the spirit aspect of it, what of it says the character is a werewolf?<br /> <br /> Third, isn't this a much better Gnawer concept? Glass Walkers are more high concept and experimental, while Gnawers are more down to earth.<br /> <br /> Fourth, all the concepts feel very lacking in the werewolf department. I know these ARE GWs and so the most human tribe, but even GWs aren't actually humans nor do they live by the rules of humanity. Glass Walkers are the wolves in sheep's clothing, but they aren't ACTUALLY sheep. Yet this preview implies they are the sheep 90% time.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T11:44:18-07:00","id":1509756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509746#post1509746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering lupus is no longer a statted thing, I find it interesting how the preview STILL takes time to say GWs don't have many of them.<br /> <br /> To the other stuff; As Knightingale above said, the example characters seem very much like 'doing a hobby in-between jobs.' Also, given how W5 sounds like, the emphasis on GWs choosing to side with humans sounds a bit weird.<br /> <br /> All in all, I find this preview a bit too surface level and non-indicative.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the lupus-thing, I'm also thinking: So it says &quot;a number that dwindles daily&quot;. Okay... How? With the Garou-Kin-dynamic the only thing that matters is the amount of wolf-kin out there and whether they found their way into the Glass Walker Tribe. So how does the number of wolfborn get less...? It means at one point there was a certain number of wolf-kin who resonated enough with the Spider-Patron-Spirit to become Glass Walkers and now there are less of them.<br /> <br /> Additionally, that write-up feels like someone is subconsciously still writing it like it's the old WtA-model. In the Garou-Kin-model membership-numbers are linked to how many you get to recruit plus how how many Kin resonate with a Patron-Spirit and join a Tribe without being influenced by someone who's already a Garou. I don't really feel like that write-up has shifted gears in how this is talked about...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fourth, all the concepts feel very lacking in the werewolf department. I know these ARE GWs and so the most human tribe, but even GWs aren't actually humans nor do they live by the rules of humanity. Glass Walkers are the wolves in sheep's clothing, but they aren't ACTUALLY sheep. Yet this preview implies they are the sheep 90% time.\u200b </div> </div> </div>I had the same feeling there as you. Especially rereading them... You read these archetypes and I don't think anybody without context would know that these are supposed to be werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T11:58:31-07:00","id":1509757,"title":"","content":"If 'build' encompasses 'make it do something it shouldn't', which I'd have called Exploit, it might work. It still pushes Glasswalkers towards being techies carrying a lot of parts around with them, which is a somewhat narrow view of the tribe, but maybe we'll get additional Favours when they publish a Player's Guide in 2028.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T12:07:11-07:00","id":1509758,"title":"","content":"Yeah if you gave these descriptions to a person and asked if what kind of supernatural they are, the person would just say they are job descriptions. The only one that talks about spirits at all is the &quot;Car Liberator&quot; which has it's own problems as mentioned. And the tattoo artist whole thing about 'putting their legend on their body' is neat but, it doesn't really do a good job about making it tied to the tribe's ideas as a whole.<br /> <br /> The only one that <i>feels</i> Glass Walker is the Urban Planner but, that's only because it seems like something Spider would say is good. &quot;Make the Web perfect so that prey get perfect trapped while everything else flows through&quot; or something. This does come back to the point to what do any of these mean to any of their Verbs or Spider in particular. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T12:30:16-07:00","id":1509762,"title":"","content":"I looked at some V5 archetypes, because I was curious if this mostly human focus is WoD5 in general.<br /> <br /> These are ones for Tzimisce (a good comparison since Tzimi are pretty inhuman):Landlord, Gang Leader, Grudgebearer and Special Forces Commander.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, minus the last ones, these sound very Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Of course these ARE GWs, so maybe the other tribes are a bit less human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T12:42:24-07:00","id":1509763,"title":"","content":"Like looking at the archetypes you can make a case for these to match a verb. So Detective is research, Urban Planner is build, you can make a case of Car Liberator for repurpose, but there is no hack. Which is very odd since out of all the verbs that is the most pointed to Glass Walkers as a tribe that set them apart from all others. Why do we have no Cyber Security Agent?<br /> <br /> I wish they they made the descriptions more about the verbs and their relationship to Spider. Like if the Car Liberator talked about how Spider wants to you trap tainted machines in order to take them apart to given them a new place in the web and to the Car Liberator a tainted machine are cars that under those people that mistreat them. Like an idea is there that <i>could</i> be tied better to what they want to do but, instead they talk about being a Robin Hood and Crimes.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T12:53:44-07:00","id":1509765,"title":"","content":"Considering that V5 is focused on Neonates and Fledglings 'what is/was your human job' is very appropriate. Most are probably still defining their identity by their human job even if they aren't still doing it, and may in fact have been embraced specifically because of it. For Garou under the pre-W5 model it makes little sense, most Garou change early enjoy that they'll be defined by their role in werewolf society, but maybe it is just a Glasswalkers thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm still upset that Cockroach lost his spot to a bloody Weaver totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T12:55:33-07:00","id":1509766,"title":"","content":"So, I think that each of the concepts is actually embodying a Verb.<ul><li><i>Build</i> - Tatoo Artist - creating something new and using it to record what the Garou need to know</li> <li><i>Hack</i> - Urban Planner - hacking the system from within and turning it towards the Garou needs</li> <li><i>Repurpose</i> - The Car Liberator - Taking from the Rich and Giving to the poor</li> <li><i>Research</i> - Detective - the description is almost creepy in the fact that the character NEEDS to know rather than actually use it as a means to an end</li> </ul>The description is rather unfocused and invoking a lot of setting elements that we don't have a context for right now, and which I'm not even sure we'll have context without what we know about the old games. There's also the fact that without the societies of the Tribes they're probably the resident &quot;human&quot; tribe. The general description was serviceable if confusing until they got to the ban and the Patron.<br /> <br /> The new Glass Walkers seem to be<b> Bob the Builder </b>Tribe of the game. And not just that but they cannot destroy technology without seriously hampering themselves. I'm willing to interpret their perk a bit more generously by saying that building things doesn't necessarily mean items, it could mean organizations and processes. Sadly limiting it to those specific skills does torpedo that sentiment quite quickly. As for the Spider... it's a new interpretation of Spider as the Great Builder, not the usual Naturae Spider. It seems to be very Weavery in its agenda and could even be an aspect of the Weaver. I don't think this choice was well thought through.<br /> <br /> As for the sample characters - there is little that makes them work within the tribe or within a pack, they are all standalone concepts and lack hooks into the setting. This is something that was often considered a weakness in old Werewolf - it was a setting that was always lore havy and required a lot of thought to make concepts that hook into the setting as presented. I assume that's the main reason they went for this. I still believe it could have been done better to give a link between their jobs as Garou and their passions/jobs (!?!?).<br /> <br /> As I mentioned I find the detective freaky. The Tatoo Artist is a missed opportunity where they could have built him up as someone making tatoo fetishes and talens, and where his personal tatoos could be stories like Maui's Tatoos in Moana. The Car Liberator is ridiculous for being this grungy rebel type that's sneering at people for judging him, if anything he utterly screams 90s with that attitude. The Urban planner could be interesting, but feels a bit shallow without further context and especially without knowing how hard normal life and jobs are for the new Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T13:03:32-07:00","id":1509767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509766#post1509766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I think that each of the concepts is actually embodying a Verb.<ul><li><i>Build</i> - Tatoo Artist - creating something new and using it to record what the Garou need to know</li> <li><i>Hack</i> - Urban Planner - hacking the system from within and turning it towards the Garou needs</li> <li><i>Repurpose</i> - The Car Liberator - Taking from the Rich and Giving to the poor</li> <li><i>Research</i> - Detective - the description is almost creepy in the fact that the character NEEDS to know rather than actually use it as a means to an end</li> </ul>The description is rather unfocused and invoking a lot of setting elements that we don't have a context for right now, and which I'm not even sure we'll have context without what we know about the old games. There's also the fact that without the societies of the Tribes they're probably the resident &quot;human&quot; tribe. The general description was serviceable if confusing until they got to the ban and the Patron.<br /> <br /> The new Glass Walkers seem to be<b> Bob the Builder </b>Tribe of the game. And not just that but they cannot destroy technology without seriously hampering themselves. I'm willing to interpret their perk a bit more generously by saying that building things doesn't necessarily mean items, it could mean organizations and processes. Sadly limiting it to those specific skills does torpedo that sentiment quite quickly. As for the Spider... it's a new interpretation of Spider as the Great Builder, not the usual Naturae Spider. It seems to be very Weavery in its agenda and could even be an aspect of the Weaver. I don't think this choice was well thought through.<br /> <br /> As for the sample characters - there is little that makes them work within the tribe or within a pack, they are all standalone concepts and lack hooks into the setting. This is something that was often considered a weakness in old Werewolf - it was a setting that was always lore havy and required a lot of thought to make concepts that hook into the setting as presented. I assume that's the main reason they went for this. I still believe it could have been done better to give a link between their jobs as Garou and their passions/jobs (!?!?).<br /> <br /> As I mentioned I find the detective freaky. The Tatoo Artist is a missed opportunity where they could have built him up as someone making tatoo fetishes and talens, and where his personal tatoos could be stories like Maui's Tatoos in Moana. The Car Liberator is ridiculous for being this grungy rebel type that's sneering at people for judging him, if anything he utterly screams 90s with that attitude. The Urban planner could be interesting, but feels a bit shallow without further context and especially without knowing how hard normal life and jobs are for the new Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Asking as a relativenewbie. How much &quot;Fight he Power &quot; energy did early Wod have? Would the car liberator who believes stealing a car is ok because he's stealing from someone rich enough to buy another car fit in in the early days?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 04-26-2023, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T13:14:41-07:00","id":1509769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509766#post1509766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new Glass Walkers seem to be<b> Bob the Builder </b>Tribe of the game. And not just that but they cannot destroy technology without seriously hampering themselves. I'm willing to interpret their perk a bit more generously by saying that building things doesn't necessarily mean items, it could mean organizations and processes. Sadly limiting it to those specific skills does torpedo that sentiment quite quickly. As for the Spider... it's a new interpretation of Spider as the Great Builder, not the usual Naturae Spider. It seems to be very Weavery in its agenda and could even be an aspect of the Weaver. I don't think this choice was well thought through.</div> </div> </div> </div>It said in the previews that the goal of the change was to create a more direct link between the Glass Walkers and the Weaver. So, you're right in saying that it &quot;seeam very Weavery&quot;. That was the intent. The idea is that this is what creates tensions between Glass Walkers and other Tribes.<br /> <br /> I get how this approach of giving every Tribe this very different approach/outlook is the explanation for the fissures which will lead to the downfall of the Garou-Nation in the status-quo of W5 - but stuff like this makes me wonder instead how was there a Garou-Nation to begin with...?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T13:18:13-07:00","id":1509771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509769#post1509769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It said in the previews that the goal of the change was to create a more direct link between the Glass Walkers and the Weaver. So, you're right in saying that it &quot;seeam very Weavery&quot;. That was the intent. The idea is that this is what creates tensions between Glass Walkers and other Tribes.<br /> <br /> I get how this approach of giving every Tribe this very different approach/outlook is the explanation for the fissures which will lead to the downfall of the Garou-Nation in the status-quo of W5 - but stuff like this makes me wonder instead how was there a Garou-Nation to begin with...?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My theory is that the &quot;Garou Nation&quot; in w5 like a country. All countries large and small have many different groups in it and many of those groups have incompatible goals,but there's always someone saying the groups have to work together for &quot;the country's goals&quot;.<br /> that's what the Garou Nation is in w5,more of an ideal even in its heyday than an actual formal organization <br /> Just my theory of course","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T13:25:44-07:00","id":1509772,"title":"","content":"I personally don't really think that the writers wanted to tie each archetype to one of the verbs. I was just using it as an example of why I find Tattoo Artist odd in the bunch and the fact that there is no tech based archetype kind of sad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509766#post1509766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tatoo Artist is a missed opportunity where they could have built him up as someone making tatoo fetishes and talens, and where his personal tatoos could be stories like Maui's Tatoos in Moana.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I love this concept and have used it before in games (both as a player and ST.) I doesn't really scream &quot;Glass Walker&quot; to me. I don't really see other tribe like saying no to having ritual scaring that eventual went to tattoos. To use your example I wouldn't say Maui is more Glass Walker then any other tribe.<br /> <br /> I think a better &quot;Repurpose&quot; would be a regular mechanic or maybe something like those guys that find junkers and restore them. Taking the crime angle here just muddies the water for what they want to be and show for this character idea.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T13:27:03-07:00","id":1509773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509771#post1509771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My theory is that the &quot;Garou Nation&quot; in w5 like a country. All countries large and small have many different groups in it and many of those groups have incompatible goals,but there's always someone saying the groups have to work together for &quot;the country's goals&quot;.<br /> that's what the Garou Nation is in w5,more of an ideal even in its heyday than an actual formal organization<br /> Just my theory of course</div> </div> </div> </div>And I would've accepted that. Most of the lore has been thrown out and so when it says in the Lexicon from the Introduction we've seen it's a &quot;loose union of Tribes&quot;, it's just that we're now emphasizing the word &quot;loose&quot; there with how the Garou-Nation could function in the good old days but crisis and the need to act in unison has led to its downfall instead. Or something like that.<br /> <br /> But the Lexicon also still has the Impergium listed. And that means at one point the Garou-Nation was able to act in unison in culling humans. Also, now that I think about it... How does that work with a Garou/Kin-dynamic...? Aren't there random humans at random times still experiencing their First Change...? In this scenario, mass-killing humans means potentially killing Kin. I wonder if the writers have considered this or subconsciously are presenting the Impergium like it's still old WtA...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T13:28:46-07:00","id":1509774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509773#post1509773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I would've accepted that. Most of the lore has been thrown out and so when it says in the Lexicon from the Introduction we've seen it's a &quot;loose union of Tribes&quot;, it's just that we're now emphasizing the word &quot;loose&quot; there with how the Garou-Nation could function in the good old days but crisis and the need to act in unison has led to its downfall instead. Or something like that.<br /> <br /> But the Lexicon also still has the Impergium listed. And that means at one point the Garou-Nation was able to act in unison in culling humans. Also, now that I think about it... How does that work with a Garou/Kin-dynamic...? Aren't there random humans at random times still experiencing their First Change...? In this scenario, mass-killing humans means potentially killing Kin. I wonder if the writers have considered this or subconsciously are presenting the Impergium like it's still old WtA...?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good criticisms. I suspect the Impergium might have been recontextualized","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T13:32:00-07:00","id":1509776,"title":"","content":"Weren't Glasswalkers generally more about the Wyld side of technology. The eternally updating, changing, always something new side, with Tribe leadership changing as new trends in technology and human culture strengthening or weakening Clans. The Glasswalkers weren't just taking Weaver approved technology that did they job, they were putting up signal towers in the Umbra, writing their own software, and flashing the BIOS on their phones because there's a new and better version to use.<br /> <br /> Then not having a Weaver totem was <i>very</i> intentional from both an IC and OOC viewpoint. They knew they risked falling to the Weaver and weren't stupid enough to head closer to the line with no reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T13:35:52-07:00","id":1509777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509772#post1509772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I love this concept and have used it before in games (both as a player and ST.) I doesn't really scream &quot;Glass Walker&quot; to me. I don't really see other tribe like saying no to having ritual scaring that eventual went to tattoos. To use your example I wouldn't say Maui is more Glass Walker then any other tribe.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I agree with you. The trick here is that these are just generic urban stereotypes. GW's are now the Urban Man / Gap Tribe.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T07:01:27-07:00","id":1509954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1509777#post1509777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I agree with you. The trick here is that these are just generic urban stereotypes. GW's are now the Urban Man / Gap Tribe.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-jxJDEj5a_8\" target=\"_blank\">Magic City Man</a> here we go!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T09:47:24-07:00","id":1510613,"title":"","content":"<img width=\"1280\" height=\"819\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/3wbb8MB.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/3wbb8MB.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/3wbb8MB.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Here we go! First actual look on social structures of W5!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T10:10:28-07:00","id":1510616,"title":"","content":"One thing that I feel has been missing in all the previews so far is to talk about how much being a Garou is a communal experience. Moots and Septs are mentioned in the Lexicon of the introduction but whenever the Garou-existence is discussed the highest social order that gets discussed is the Pack you're a part of. The Pack-descriptions feel more like VtM-Anarch-Coteries with some Garou-flavor. Especially &quot;Party Animals&quot;... that one feels very much like a VtM-group-concept.<br /> <br /> And this kinda confirms that W5 won't try to do anything similar to the Coterie-system of V5. I'm really curious how that Caern-system will look like as that's essentially the replacement for it (according to the previews).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T11:04:24-07:00","id":1510622,"title":"","content":"And we run into the first contradiction; The GW preview hinted GWs manage human society just fine, but here it is outright stated that most garou do not vibe with humanity.<br /> <br /> Also, I know I'm starting to sound like a broken record, but this reads like Forsaken core's info on packs. To the point that deednames are self-chosen monikers. There is nothing wrong with that in practice, but WtF and W5 are still supposed to be different games.<br /> <br /> I get that W5 is trying to be more of a ground up type of game, but it should find its own way to be that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T13:12:51-07:00","id":1510629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510622#post1510622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we run into the first contradiction; The GW preview hinted GWs manage human society just fine, but here it is outright stated that most garou do not vibe with humanity.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How are you supposed to be 'street' if you're disconnected from humanity? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T13:38:07-07:00","id":1510632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510629#post1510629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How are you supposed to be 'street' if you're disconnected from humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Easily, you mimic humanity. You keep your distance but also watch them intently. That is how GWs have been ( at least for me), not human but instead interested in how humans do things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T13:52:54-07:00","id":1510636,"title":"","content":"Part of the assumption in the tribe name of &quot;Glass Walkers&quot; is that they don't quite walk directly among humanity, but watch over them from the tops of buildings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T15:16:22-07:00","id":1510644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510622#post1510622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we run into the first contradiction; The GW preview hinted GWs manage human society just fine, but here it is outright stated that most garou do not vibe with humanity.<br /> <br /> Also, I know I'm starting to sound like a broken record, but this reads like Forsaken core's info on packs. To the point that deednames are self-chosen monikers. There is nothing wrong with that in practice, but WtF and W5 are still supposed to be different games.<br /> <br /> I get that W5 is trying to be more of a ground up type of game, but it should find its own way to be that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> GWs are and were the exception to the rule even before, though. It's not a contradiction, so far, only a partial view. I mean, the other Garous suspect them of having betrayed the Nation during the Impergium!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T15:32:35-07:00","id":1510645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510644#post1510644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> GWs are and were the exception to the rule even before, though. It's not a contradiction, so far, only a partial view. I mean, the other Garous suspect them of having betrayed the Nation during the Impergium!</div> </div> </div> </div>They were not an exception, they just had ways to hide themselves among humanity. A huge point in the revised tribebook is that living in a city is a struggle for even GWs and theytend to have very high willpower due to that.<br /> <br /> Scaring humanity is a species trait for garou, as if their Rage. The GWs don't get to ignore it just because they live in cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T21:25:34-07:00","id":1510674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510632#post1510632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Easily, you mimic humanity. You keep your distance but also watch them intently. That is how GWs have been ( at least for me), not human but instead interested in how humans do things.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty restrictive approach, especially considering how everything else in the setting appears to be trimmed back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T21:53:49-07:00","id":1510675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510674#post1510674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a pretty restrictive approach, especially considering how everything else in the setting appears to be trimmed back.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how the preview above words it, giving Glass Walkers a free pass would be counter to the point of the sidebar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T21:59:21-07:00","id":1510676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510675#post1510675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is how the preview above words it, giving Glass Walkers a free pass would be counter to the point of the sidebar.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I meant for werewolves in general, this game is proposed to be grounded in 'street' ground floor universe but then says werewolves are disconnected to humanity, this gets especially odd considering they're probably bringing in touchstones. Aside from feeling very cofd it doesn't seem to really click with the outline of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T23:17:17-07:00","id":1510681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510676#post1510676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No I meant for werewolves in general, this game is proposed to be grounded in 'street' ground floor universe but then says werewolves are disconnected to humanity, this gets especially odd considering they're probably bringing in touchstones. Aside from feeling very cofd it doesn't seem to really click with the outline of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it doesn't. But this is nothing new in the WtA world as many times the corebooks go deep into why garou cannot have jobs and then later books or the cor itself subverts it.<br /> <br /> I find it funny that no one caught this when setting up the previews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T11:10:10-07:00","id":1510713,"title":"","content":"If we're talking about contradictions... In that latest preview you have that section called &quot;Finding The Pack&quot; and yet... it never even talks about how one finds a Pack as a Garou. It's about Pack-dynamics... sort-of. And finding a Pack would be an interesting topic actually in this mid-Apocalypse-setting where the Garou-Nation has fallen apart. So it's weird that it's instead about how in Garou-legends a Pack has one of each Auspice but in reality it doesn't (and I feel like there are way too many words spent on communicating that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T14:49:37-07:00","id":1510720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510713#post1510713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're talking about contradictions... In that latest preview you have that section called &quot;Finding The Pack&quot; and yet... it never even talks about how one finds a Pack as a Garou. It's about Pack-dynamics... sort-of. And finding a Pack would be an interesting topic actually in this mid-Apocalypse-setting where the Garou-Nation has fallen apart. So it's weird that it's instead about how in Garou-legends a Pack has one of each Auspice but in reality it doesn't (and I feel like there are way too many words spent on communicating that).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally just 2 pages, there might be another 15 about Packs, as far as we know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T02:20:13-07:00","id":1510762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510720#post1510720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's literally just 2 pages, there might be another 15 about Packs, as far as we know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>15 would be a bit excessive considering there are no mechanics attached to that idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ...<br /> <br /> But my criticisms are about those two pages specifically. This is about the presentation of information, not the information itself. My criticism wouldn't change if I saw those two pages in the context of the whole book. All that could change is maybe me pointing out that there are other parts of the book that actually are about &quot;Finding a Pack&quot; whereas this section we've gotten isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T03:59:43-07:00","id":1510771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510713#post1510713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're talking about contradictions... In that latest preview you have that section called &quot;Finding The Pack&quot; and yet... it never even talks about how one finds a Pack as a Garou. It's about Pack-dynamics... sort-of. And finding a Pack would be an interesting topic actually in this mid-Apocalypse-setting where the Garou-Nation has fallen apart. So it's weird that it's instead about how in Garou-legends a Pack has one of each Auspice but in reality it doesn't (and I feel like there are way too many words spent on communicating that).</div> </div> </div> </div>I fear we might run into the Forsaken 1st edition problem of a vague starting point. I assume the pack finds the garou and makes them join.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T04:39:32-07:00","id":1510772,"title":"","content":"If garou tend to abandon their human lives, don't/can't hold down jobs for the most part, and have no kin to help support them, how the hell do they exist or function within the world at all? They can't all be pick pockets or bank robbers.<br /> <br /> This just looks like they got rid of kinfolk without thinking through what that actually means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T06:25:50-07:00","id":1510776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510772#post1510772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If garou tend to abandon their human lives, don't/can't hold down jobs for the most part, and have no kin to help support them, how the hell do they exist or function within the world at all? They can't all be pick pockets or bank robbers.<br /> <br /> This just looks like they got rid of kinfolk without thinking through what that actually means.</div> </div> </div> </div>But from what we saw in the GW preview it seems like they do/can have jobs? At least I'm not sure how to classify a Urban Planner, Tattoo Artist, or Detective if they are not &quot;jobs.&quot; Are they saying that this 'Urban Planner' just sits around think about how to design a city but then just begs on the street? I'm not saying that losing the kinfolk doesn't create even more logistical nightmares but, even within the text it seems like we are being given contradictive statements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T06:53:49-07:00","id":1510779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510776#post1510776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But from what we saw in the GW preview it seems like they do/can have jobs? At least I'm not sure how to classify a Urban Planner, Tattoo Artist, or Detective if they are not &quot;jobs.&quot; Are they saying that this 'Urban Planner' just sits around think about how to design a city but then just begs on the street? I'm not saying that losing the kinfolk doesn't create even more logistical nightmares but, even within the text it seems like we are being given contradictive statements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably by working through a series of burned out but high-WP humans that are more resistant to the Garou capacity to freak others out, to take the place of Kinfolk as intermediaries. It's kind of like the personal assistants that Dragon-Blooded pick up in Exalted, just replace the superhuman pace of the Chosen with the horror-born psychological toll of being around a monster and having it slowly dawn on someone that there's something wrong... assuming that a mockery or whatever doesn't kill them first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T07:39:16-07:00","id":1510789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510776#post1510776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But from what we saw in the GW preview it seems like they do/can have jobs? At least I'm not sure how to classify a Urban Planner, Tattoo Artist, or Detective if they are not &quot;jobs.&quot; Are they saying that this 'Urban Planner' just sits around think about how to design a city but then just begs on the street? I'm not saying that losing the kinfolk doesn't create even more logistical nightmares but, even within the text it seems like we are being given contradictive statements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had hoped they'd at least have this aspect fixed since so much of the point is street and everyday life. This is something that was legit flawed in WtA and W5 could have just straight up said garou CAN hold jobs and CAN live in society since that is the core gameplay.<br /> <br /> Keeping the isolation without kin and when most of the game is based on low-level stuff is bizarre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T08:04:48-07:00","id":1510791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510789#post1510789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping the isolation without kin and when most of the game is based on low-level stuff is bizarre.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of the bizarre decision in H5 to make it a central point of the game to condemn all hunter-orgs (and everybody who works for them) as pseudo-antagonists in a way. It's another way of forcing the game to be played in a certain way, I guess.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Packs In A Modern World&quot;-sidebar from the latest really focuses on a very particular idea of what Garou are like. There, Garou are characterized as operating on the fringes of society, mingling with disenfranchised people, hunting in the rundown parts of a city, being vigilantes and/or activists or being part of a subculture. That also contradicts this idea of the Garou-Kin-dynamic that anybody could become a Kin. Rather it feels like whoever wrote this had a very specific small set of characteristics/types of people in mind when they talked about Garou in that section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T09:11:07-07:00","id":1510796,"title":"","content":"The point of the isolation is now super, ultra, mega ANGST! Angst like you've never angsted before!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T09:26:24-07:00","id":1510798,"title":"","content":"I also feel like in the latest preview it's a bit of an understatement where in the &quot;Packs In A Modern World&quot;-sidebar it says at the end: &quot;Packs may also find that their initial concept changes over time, or when they acquire resources to protect, such as a caern that ties them to a particular location.&quot; But W5 didn't take V5's Coterie-type and turned it into an equivalent Pack-type. Instead, W5 has Caern-management-rules which makes that matter a loaded question since this makes it pretty clear what W5 thinks Packs <i>should </i>end up doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T07:45:46-07:00","id":1510882,"title":"","content":"I don't want sound grumpy but none of those material scream &quot;werewolf&quot; to me. All of this sound like Human+ stuff. You could use this material, preview, char concepts, etc. in a all humans+ PCs chronicle with a little of shamanism to the spirit stuff. Like, a motorbike club, party animals, tattoo artist...<br /> <br /> Someone here said that if you showed the image to people without context and asked their opinion they would awnser its people + job, and this is a remark I agree with. Vampires at least have the detail that their existence, life, jobs, aspirations etc all happen, and have to happen, at night (though in v5 i think they are too Human+, too).<br /> <br /> I think they are focusing too much in the extra media zone (video games and low funding series/movies/larp/podcast/twitch &quot;real playing), like, &quot;this could be a netflix series!&quot; (If this horrible explanation make any sense to you).<br /> <br /> But IDK, maybe its intentional? *shrugs*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T07:30:33-07:00","id":1510979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510771#post1510771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fear we might run into the Forsaken 1st edition problem of a vague starting point. I assume the pack finds the garou and makes them join.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coming back to this, there are of course a lot of similarities between WtF and the previews of W5 but one aspect that has always been bothered me about W5 is the worldbuilding. With WtF (even 1E) you have the excuse that Pangaea, the killing of Father Wolf and the Uratha and Pure split all come with the predicate of \u201cA long, long time ago\u2026\u201d. But the fall of the Garou-Nation, the Get and Stargazers leaving the Nation, the setting being mid-Apocalypse and Gaia being dead/dying\u2026 All of that supposedly happened in living memory. So it can\u2019t be as vague as WtF-worldbuilding and still trying to be vague creates a high likeliness for plotholes. With WtF reducing worldbuilding was easy because it restarted the whole thing with a blank slate and most of the worldbuilding happened in some mythical past. But W5 doesn\u2019t have that same luxury. Even with tossing out a ton of lore getting to the point where W5 wants to be it has to explain <i>how </i>the Garou-Nation isn\u2019t a thing anymore, for example. And not explaining it properly is a plothole in the game's worldbuilding. After all, what you're trying to explain is the past of the setting of how things went from point A to point B to point C. Being way too vague might create descriptions like going from point A to point C and just make you question the logic of the setting.<br /> <br /> The only corebook done by this particular team was H5 and the worldbuilding there is a complete mess. So I don\u2019t have very high hopes how this will get handled in the W5 corebook.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510882#post1510882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they are focusing too much in the extra media zone (video games and low funding series/movies/larp/podcast/twitch &quot;real playing), like, &quot;this could be a netflix series!&quot; (If this horrible explanation make any sense to you).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, they're trying to but H5 spawned 0 videogames so far and W5's decision to do the whole &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-thing means both Earthblood and Heartsong have nothing to do with W5. And I wonder how many videogames you will get out of W5 if the whole pitch is that is <i>not </i>the WtA you used to know. With V5 despite all its changes, there was still enough of old VtM remaining to appeal to nostalgia for old VtM. If you want to make a game about W5, you make a game <i>about W5</i>. And if you're a game-developer and a fan of WtA, it's unlikely you're gonna be happy with every change W5 has made (especially when it comes to the Tribes). So we'll see how many people will want to make games for the new W5.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T10:44:33-07:00","id":1510997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510979#post1510979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming back to this, there are of course a lot of similarities between WtF and the previews of W5 but one aspect that has always been bothered me about W5 is the worldbuilding. With WtF (even 1E) you have the excuse that Pangaea, the killing of Father Wolf and the Uratha and Pure split all come with the predicate of \u201cA long, long time ago\u2026\u201d. But the fall of the Garou-Nation, the Get and Stargazers leaving the Nation, the setting being mid-Apocalypse and Gaia being dead/dying\u2026 All of that supposedly happened in living memory. So it can\u2019t be as vague as WtF-worldbuilding and still trying to be vague creates a high likeliness for plotholes. With WtF reducing worldbuilding was easy because it restarted the whole thing with a blank slate and most of the worldbuilding happened in some mythical past. But W5 doesn\u2019t have that same luxury. Even with tossing out a ton of lore getting to the point where W5 wants to be it has to explain <i>how </i>the Garou-Nation isn\u2019t a thing anymore, for example. And not explaining it properly is a plothole in the game's worldbuilding. After all, what you're trying to explain is the past of the setting of how things went from point A to point B to point C. Being way too vague might create descriptions like going from point A to point C and just make you question the logic of the setting.<br /> <br /> The only corebook done by this particular team was H5 and the worldbuilding there is a complete mess. So I don\u2019t have very high hopes how this will get handled in the W5 corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that was not what I meant. I meant that WtF 1st ed was very vague on how one joins packs or even how one joins a tribe. With W5, I feel it is going to follow the same vague nature as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T11:00:10-07:00","id":1510999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1510997#post1510997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, that was not what I meant. I meant that WtF 1st ed was very vague on how one joins packs or even how one joins a tribe. With W5, I feel it is going to follow the same vague nature as well.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Markedly not, though funnily enough this is a point there where Second Edition is vaguer than First. Joining a pack is a matter of giving oblations to the totem and making a pact with them (Second Edition probably didn't reiterate it to make it easier to justify the human packmates, particularly the more unwitting ones), where as joining a Tribe is a Rite performed on an initiate binding them to the Firstborn (Second Edition probably didn't go into this because that's not the sort of thing most people find necessary for playability).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T23:50:55-07:00","id":1511333,"title":"","content":"During Q&amp;A session, it was mentioned that now Garou aren't inherently hate vampires. It means they just rethink their attitude after they were defeated by Wyrm, or they like &quot;always&quot; has such view?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T10:46:58-07:00","id":1511386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511333#post1511333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During Q&amp;A session, it was mentioned that now Garou aren't inherently hate vampires. It means they just rethink their attitude after they were defeated by Wyrm, or they like &quot;always&quot; has such view?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The question is for me-why wouldn't you hate vampires? They're fucking horrible especially in 5th","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T11:46:04-07:00","id":1511395,"title":"","content":"Everyone hates the vampires in the WoD... even the vampires.<br /> <br /> I have a feeling that the execution is going to be more of &quot;vampires are dangerous and horrible, but not knowingly agents of the Wyrm, better to avoid them and deal with more pressing matters,&quot; instead of the somewhat exaggerated, &quot;Leeches are Wyrm beasts, kill any you find ASAP!&quot; attitude sometimes shown in the older books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T22:25:58-07:00","id":1511427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511386#post1511386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The question is for me-why wouldn't you hate vampires? They're fucking horrible especially in 5th</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou could hate them in more reasonable way. Like mages did - a-la &quot;Bloodsuckers are deeply fucked critters, yet it's not a reason to kill them on sight.&quot; IIRC, the open war only happened between Hermetists and Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T09:20:28-07:00","id":1511457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511395#post1511395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone hates the vampires in the WoD... even the vampires.<br /> <br /> I have a feeling that the execution is going to be more of &quot;vampires are dangerous and horrible, but not knowingly agents of the Wyrm, better to avoid them and deal with more pressing matters,&quot; instead of the somewhat exaggerated, &quot;Leeches are Wyrm beasts, kill any you find ASAP!&quot; attitude sometimes shown in the older books.</div> </div> </div> </div>personally ive always gone with kill on sight rather than proactive extermination.<br /> <br /> It doesn't even really make sense since w5 is in its own universe now. You may as well just have them as wyrm fodder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T11:58:20-07:00","id":1511466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511457#post1511457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> personally ive always gone with kill on sight rather than proactive extermination.<br /> <br /> It doesn't even really make sense since w5 is in its own universe now. You may as well just have them as wyrm fodder.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Amm... how is the former better than later?<br /> 2) People gonna do crossovers anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T12:40:33-07:00","id":1511470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511333#post1511333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During Q&amp;A session, it was mentioned that now Garou aren't inherently hate vampires. It means they just rethink their attitude after they were defeated by Wyrm, or they like &quot;always&quot; has such view?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Garou apparently can't sense wyrmish corruption anymore, and there's a not insignificant argument to be made that vampires are as of the Weaver as they are of the Wyrm. They also don't tend to have similar stomping grounds, so if they're not actively hunting vampires they probably don't run into them much.<br /> <br /> So it's probably more a case of 'no special hatred, and we've got bigger problems', combined with not pissing off Vampire players. As has been said they'll probably dislike vampires as much as anybody else, but run into them less than hunters would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-12T13:57:36-07:00","id":1511478,"title":"","content":"If fomori aren't super-splatter opponents that try to divert Garou attention by numbers and vampires remain mobile centers for turning blood into an addictive, potentially debilitating drug and also terrible people who shit up their surroundings and move on to go squat in another formerly nice place, I'm not seeing why Garou wouldn't target vampires <i>more often.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T00:16:15-07:00","id":1511515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511478#post1511478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If fomori aren't super-splatter opponents that try to divert Garou attention by numbers and vampires remain mobile centers for turning blood into an addictive, potentially debilitating drug and also terrible people who shit up their surroundings and move on to go squat in another formerly nice place, I'm not seeing why Garou wouldn't target vampires <i>more often.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>How are vampires are worse than mundane drugdealers and mortals as is in this extent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T06:59:48-07:00","id":1511608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511515#post1511515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are vampires are worse than mundane drugdealers and mortals as is in this extent?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Drug dealer sells drugs and are finite, vampire hunt and kill humans indefinatly. Its a matter of scale. Its like with rudi from anarch is objectively more of a long term threat to the lgbt community than some scumbag nazi gangbanger.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T07:19:10-07:00","id":1511612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511515#post1511515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are vampires are worse than mundane drugdealers and mortals as is in this extent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they can make bad fetish porn plot-alikes pop into existence by sneaking imperceptible amounts of blood into food and drink. That's not even something they have to try to cultivate, it's part and parcel of their simple existence. When they try to go further than this, it gets even worse, since now anyone could be subverted but not know it. Not all corruption has to be in a metaphysical sense.<br /> <br /> Best to never let even a toe hold alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T07:34:34-07:00","id":1511613,"title":"","content":"Vampires to Garou have always been &quot;We may win most battles but we will absolutely lose wars&quot; Aggressively trying to remove vampires on the basis of what they are rather than what they've done is just asking to get your Caern defiled, your kin killed, and your pack mates mind-controlled. It's better to avoid the vampires entirely if you can, or be very selective and only take out the really bad ones or the fools who end up lost in the woods. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T07:50:54-07:00","id":1511614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511613#post1511613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires to Garou have always been &quot;We may win most battles but we will absolutely lose wars&quot; Aggressively trying to remove vampires on the basis of what they are rather than what they've done is just asking to get your Caern defiled, your kin killed, and your pack mates mind-controlled. It's better to avoid the vampires entirely if you can, or be very selective and only take out the really bad ones or the fools who end up lost in the woods.</div> </div> </div> </div> Pretty much yeah, pick of the ones who won't be missed or the ones who draw a bullseye on their back.<br /> <br /> As a side I'd forgotten how great garou are as horror antagonists for vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T11:06:19-07:00","id":1511630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a side I'd forgotten how great garou are as horror antagonists for vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and how pathetic they are whe it comes to actuall crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T11:45:04-07:00","id":1511634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511613#post1511613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires to Garou have always been &quot;We may win most battles but we will absolutely lose wars&quot; Aggressively trying to remove vampires on the basis of what they are rather than what they've done is just asking to get your Caern defiled, your kin killed, and your pack mates mind-controlled. It's better to avoid the vampires entirely if you can, or be very selective and only take out the really bad ones or the fools who end up lost in the woods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that in W5, there are no kinfolk and you can pin an awful lot of attacks on whatever the Fenrir are getting renamed (if they indeed are). Which is good, because a lot of the vampires doing the worst things are the ones with the most influence. Use the threat of the &quot;Fenrir&quot; to lure their forces out, and either annihilate them yourself, or leave them to the &quot;Fenrir&quot; and pick off any witnesses that would tell the vampires what's actually going on.<br /> <br /> [/Just Shadow Lord Stuff]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T12:15:43-07:00","id":1511638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511634#post1511634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that in W5, there are no kinfolk and you can pin an awful lot of attacks on whatever the Fenrir are getting renamed (if they indeed are). Which is good, because a lot of the vampires doing the worst things are the ones with the most influence. Use the threat of the &quot;Fenrir&quot; to lure their forces out, and either annihilate them yourself, or leave them to the &quot;Fenrir&quot; and pick off any witnesses that would tell the vampires what's actually going on.<br /> <br /> [/Just Shadow Lord Stuff]</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the all of 20+ years of the WoD history Parawolves never gave Garou really serious and impressive victory over vampires. We have only very, VERY vague story about ShuHorus vs Sutech. And probablyRed Moon Rising adventure.<br /> p.S. And that's exactly why a Garou (anyone of them) deserves to be yortured Ramsay Bton-style. Till s/he/them will be turned into Reek<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T02:55:39-07:00","id":1511705,"title":"","content":"I think you're simultaneously downplaying a vampire's ability to investigate (though it has been weakened significantly in 5th; I would wager Werewolves will get significant nerfs to match) whilst also being very generous with a vampire's ability to be discriminate and take insults. If I were an elder of some influence and found my childer dead as part of some werewolf pogrom, I would at least manipulate the police or kidnap someone's kid while I lobby the prince or other vampires to take action. Maybe I'll offer a bounty on wolf pelts. You just can't show weakness and let the wolves win. Fasttrack some urban expansion if I really was at a political disadvantage and could only afford to be petty. In more liberal scenarios or where other elders have had their childer touch we could send wave after wave of bling'd up soldiers at the sept or orchestrate an ecological disaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T03:51:44-07:00","id":1511707,"title":"","content":"Because of course the average vampire is a connected master planner. The biggest problem werewolves present to vampires is that they can easily kill them wrecking their plans and their perk of longevity. Sure they can fuck werewolves up, but at the end of day, the losses you incur in it can be unmanageable. It's better to let things go than escalate into Mutually assured Destruction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T05:06:53-07:00","id":1511714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511707#post1511707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because of course the average vampire is a connected master planner. The biggest problem werewolves present to vampires is that they can easily kill them wrecking their plans and their perk of longevity. Sure they can fuck werewolves up, but at the end of day, the losses you incur in it can be unmanageable. It's better to let things go than escalate into Mutually assured Destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't recall any significant of Garou in canon. Did they ever cleanse any city from vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T05:54:07-07:00","id":1511719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511705#post1511705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're simultaneously downplaying a vampire's ability to investigate (though it has been weakened significantly in 5th; I would wager Werewolves will get significant nerfs to match) whilst also being very generous with a vampire's ability to be discriminate and take insults. If I were an elder of some influence and found my childer dead as part of some werewolf pogrom, I would at least manipulate the police or kidnap someone's kid while I lobby the prince or other vampires to take action. Maybe I'll offer a bounty on wolf pelts. You just can't show weakness and let the wolves win. Fasttrack some urban expansion if I really was at a political disadvantage and could only afford to be petty. In more liberal scenarios or where other elders have had their childer touch we could send wave after wave of bling'd up soldiers at the sept or orchestrate an ecological disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that W5 loosened up the association with actual wolves significantly, and made it as likely that someone had a family as it was that they were completely alone before becoming a werewolf. They all might be completely alone except for other werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T20:52:21-07:00","id":1511768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511515#post1511515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are vampires are worse than mundane drugdealers and mortals as is in this extent?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the bloke down the road who sells pot hasn't eaten, enslaved or raped anyone in the last week which are essentially nightly activities for your average set of teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T21:18:45-07:00","id":1511770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511705#post1511705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're simultaneously downplaying a vampire's ability to investigate (though it has been weakened significantly in 5th; I would wager Werewolves will get significant nerfs to match) whilst also being very generous with a vampire's ability to be discriminate and take insults. If I were an elder of some influence and found my childer dead as part of some werewolf pogrom, I would at least manipulate the police or kidnap someone's kid while I lobby the prince or other vampires to take action. Maybe I'll offer a bounty on wolf pelts. You just can't show weakness and let the wolves win. Fasttrack some urban expansion if I really was at a political disadvantage and could only afford to be petty. In more liberal scenarios or where other elders have had their childer touch we could send wave after wave of bling'd up soldiers at the sept or orchestrate an ecological disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of that can be pretty hard. How will anyone identify who the giant 9 foot tall fur covered werewolf's kid or family is. Are they even in the same city? In older Werewolf editions, those kinfolk likely had strong ties of people looking out for each other with can make going after one of them difficult. <br /> <br /> Ultimately in VtM, vampires are presented as living in city-cages. They control the cities, but the places outside of the cities are controlled by lupines. Vampires tend to be given warnings about heading out there and getting killed. There's also the big issue that a vampire who decides to go to war with the lupines is largely going to be on his or her own. Werewolves work together, but a vampire who spends his resources and power warring against werewolves will likely end up getting taken out by a rival. The biggest threat to a vampire is another vampire. I suspect that most vampires (even elders) who have a childe or ally get killed by a werewolf would ultimately just write it off as bad luck, rather than spending their time and resources warring with werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T22:46:05-07:00","id":1511772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511466#post1511466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Amm... how is the former better than later?<br /> 2) People gonna do crossovers anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) better is the wrong word its more realpolitik and strategy.<br /> <br /> 2) more power to them but palling around with vtm vampires is genrally a bad idea in setting and in a pure werewolf theirs zero incentive to portray them as sympathetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-16-2023, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T17:27:11-07:00","id":1512063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511772#post1511772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u20262) more power to them but palling around with vtm vampires is genrally a bad idea in setting and in a pure werewolf theirs zero incentive to portray them as sympathetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we sure about that though? I heard from a few sources leeches were no longer considered to be of the wyrm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T18:20:13-07:00","id":1512070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512063#post1512063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we sure about that though? I heard from a few sources leeches were no longer considered to be of the wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just confusion about what matters, which, coming even from the top writers and developer, does not bode well for the game. If you do bad shit, the banes will notice; if you keep doing bad shit, they'll flock to you. If there's a cloud of banes joyously swirling about someone, it really doesn't matter if they would register to Sense Wyrm in the older versions of the game or not, that's a flag so red that it bleeds, and it wouldn't be reasonable to stay around this individual for any length of time. Indeed, that just moved to the top of your priority list, if you're Garou or one of the Fera.<br /> <br /> So if vampires feed banes with suffering every moment that they exist, all the nonsense about &quot;not being of the Wyrm&quot; doesn't matter. They've made themselves of the Wyrm, even if there's no supernatural sense for it, due to what they've done. W5 has just cut out the middleman and removed any notion of supernatural resonance from the equation. Which is going to bad damned awkward if Mage adds that sort of thing back in, but this edition is what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T21:20:44-07:00","id":1512083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512063#post1512063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we sure about that though? I heard from a few sources leeches were no longer considered to be of the wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats what parawolf say but you're missing my point. My point is vampires are so awful that werewolves have very little reason to react well to them even if they're not litterally wyrm tainted. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T22:00:11-07:00","id":1512084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512083#post1512083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats what parawolf say but you're missing my point. My point is vampires are so awful that werewolves have very little reason to react well to them even if they're not litterally wyrm tainted.</div> </div> </div> </div>High-humanity vampires aren't that bad. As for werewolves, they are far from paragons of justice to judge there. And W5 Garou understand this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T11:45:34-07:00","id":1512128,"title":"","content":"Uh, while I myself enjoy high humanity vampires, &quot;dark grey morality&quot; and am in favour of an interpretation where the evils of vampire is largely a societal problem (and that if we're going to declare things undeserving of existence due to being sustained by exploitation, death and suffering, we may as well dropkick the entirety of existence into Oblivion/the Wyrm's jaws/whatever...)<br /> <br /> ...but the baseline is canon, and in canon high humanity is rare, and whether they're inherently evil or not, the vast majority of vampires are choosing to be a massive, unrepentant, miserable blight upon the world. The Garou aren't angels, but they are better for the world than vampires. Removing supernatural corruption is a good thing, regardless of if the wolfmen responsible are problematic.<br /> Furthermore, high humanity vampires generally don't have anything to fear from the Garou anyway because they don't carry a sense of the wyrm and to maintain that humanity they avoid doing things that would result in growing taint and banes (no crime, no injury to others, no minor selfish acts, no selfish <i>thoughts</i>), so the only ones in danger are the assholes who are sadly having done unto them as they do unto others.<br /> <br /> Basically, put a Garou and the average vampire in a scenario where they're surrounded by corruption and misery.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThe vampire asks; &quot;how can I make this profit me?&quot;<br /> The werewolf tries to fix it. Perhaps uses the wrong tools, perhaps fucks up, but that's certainly an improvement over deciding to maintain or worsen the situation, which is what the kindred will generally do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-19-2023, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T12:57:31-07:00","id":1512134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512084#post1512084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> High-humanity vampires aren't that bad. As for werewolves, they are far from paragons of justice to judge there. And W5 Garou understand this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhhh, maybe? And high humanity vampires are as common as effective werewolves especially in 5th. The vampire race collectively remains an absolute blight on the world.<br /> <br /> Also how do you know Mr vampire is a nice guy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-19-2023, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T13:44:07-07:00","id":1512142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512084#post1512084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> High-humanity vampires aren't that bad. As for werewolves, they are far from paragons of justice to judge there. And W5 Garou understand this.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;These imperfect actors are imperfect, and therefore as bad as the blood-drinkers that treat people as food and use everyone as tools for their gratification.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T14:18:18-07:00","id":1512147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512084#post1512084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> High-humanity vampires aren't that bad. As for werewolves, they are far from paragons of justice to judge there. And W5 Garou understand this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> garou don't pretend to be about justice, but about trying to preserve the balance of a broken cosmos.<br /> <br /> And in such a view, vampires are fundamentally damaging. They eat people, they can and will mentally enslaves them, they will sabotage societies so that they can play their games of power without human interference.<br /> <br /> Without vampires, the wod would, within universe, be better on all levels.<br /> <br /> Justice is an afterthough. The world is damaged and dying and vampires cannot help but be part of the factors that worsen this situation. Is it fair for vampires, who didn't asked their state of being? No. But fairness and justice hardly matters when the fate of reality itself is at risk.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T14:32:34-07:00","id":1512150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1511770#post1511770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of that can be pretty hard. How will anyone identify who the giant 9 foot tall fur covered werewolf's kid or family is. Are they even in the same city? In older Werewolf editions, those kinfolk likely had strong ties of people looking out for each other with can make going after one of them difficult.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually pretty easy. All you need is a vampirix investigator with just auspex 2 and animalism 4, auspex 2 and dominate 5, or just auspex 5.<br /> <br /> So you identify people that turn into giant 9 foot tall fur covered werewolves with auspex 2 thanks to their bright aura. Then you follow them, even by day, by possessing humans, flying animals, or with your astral form. You then confirm or infirm whenether the bright aura guy is a werewolf, and you start taking notes of their contacts, which allows you to draw a picture of their relation.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200bYou then repeat with every werewolf you find, and you draw a map of their social surroundings. And you can then act accordingly.<br /> <br /> For that feat, I would favorise the auspex 2 animalism 4 combinaison, and auspex 5, as a weird human following you is suspicious for a garou. A raven doing so is less strange, and the garou may not notice immediatly a strange spirit form around and understand that it's not your standard spirit.<br /> <br /> That can also be done in conjunction with your local tremere/other blood sorcerer. They could detect caerns. They could also, when the aforementioned spy gets the names of the werewolves, uses the blood mirror ritual to follow them at a distance, identifying their friends and families.<br /> <br /> And then, once you have a good picture of the garous, their caern and kinfolks, you can try to capture a kinfolk, brainwash them with dominate or the blood bond, or both, to gain all the lacking information. Then use them as troy horses.<br /> <br /> You could also kidnap the specific kinfolk of one garou, and blackmail said garou to sabotage their sept, or else soemthing really bad will happens to their loved ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> And vampires are supposed to be masters at such manipulations, it's how they deal with humans, so it's not unexpected they would do as well for garou <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T15:11:38-07:00","id":1512152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512150#post1512150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's actually pretty easy. All you need is a vampirix investigator with just auspex 2 and animalism 4, auspex 2 and dominate 5, or just auspex 5.<br /> <br /> So you identify people that turn into giant 9 foot tall fur covered werewolves with auspex 2 thanks to their bright aura. Then you follow them, even by day, by possessing humans, flying animals, or with your astral form. You then confirm or infirm whenether the bright aura guy is a werewolf, and you start taking notes of their contacts, which allows you to draw a picture of their relation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Good thing I specified Shadow Lords - Aura of Confidence renders the Garou's aura unreadable. It's a Gift that has a fairly good chance of going forward into a new edition, since it syncs up with a Vampire mechanic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b\u200bYou then repeat with every werewolf you find, and you draw a map of their social surroundings. And you can then act accordingly.<br /> <br /> For that feat, I would favorise the auspex 2 animalism 4 combinaison, and auspex 5, as a weird human following you is suspicious for a garou. A raven doing so is less strange, and the garou may not notice immediatly a strange spirit form around and understand that it's not your standard spirit. </div> </div> </div>Auspex 5 kicks you into the Dark Umbra according to W:tA's SOP, so unless they're familiar with ghosts and dead things, it wouldn't necessarily be noticeable... but you also might not be able to keep as close a watch on them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That can also be done in conjunction with your local tremere/other blood sorcerer. They could detect caerns. They could also, when the aforementioned spy gets the names of the werewolves, uses the blood mirror ritual to follow them at a distance, identifying their friends and families. </div> </div> </div>That can be fouled with some simple operational precautions that anyone in a conspiracy might use, though. Just don't meet with those people while you're trying to do dirty deeds. At least, not in the waking world; dream communication would be a bit harder to set up, but it would also not be traceable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And then, once you have a good picture of the garous, their caern and kinfolks, you can try to capture a kinfolk, brainwash them with dominate or the blood bond, or both, to gain all the lacking information. Then use them as troy horses. </div> </div> </div>Again, this is W5 I was proposing the plan for. That means there are no kinfolk, and they might not even have a caern. Also, you might end up picking up on some actual Fenrir-to-whatever while randomly reading auras, which would potentially throw you off the trail... or place you near a bloodthirsty maniac with no compunctions about tearing you to pieces in the middle of a crowd.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could also kidnap the specific kinfolk of one garou, and blackmail said garou to sabotage their sept, or else soemthing really bad will happens to their loved ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> And vampires are supposed to be masters at such manipulations, it's how they deal with humans, so it's not unexpected they would do as well for garou </div> </div> </div>Any one can play dirty, and it's not like Garou don't or won't have ways to clamp down on vampires. Bonus: most vampires won't be expecting it if their attention is fixed on werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T16:47:48-07:00","id":1512159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512150#post1512150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's actually pretty easy. All you need is a vampirix investigator with just auspex 2 and animalism 4, auspex 2 and dominate 5, or just auspex 5.<br /> <br /> So you identify people that turn into giant 9 foot tall fur covered werewolves with auspex 2 thanks to their bright aura. Then you follow them, even by day, by possessing humans, flying animals, or with your astral form. You then confirm or infirm whenether the bright aura guy is a werewolf, and you start taking notes of their contacts, which allows you to draw a picture of their relation.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200bYou then repeat with every werewolf you find, and you draw a map of their social surroundings. And you can then act accordingly.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually sounds incredible time intensive and it seems like whoever is doing that would need to spend a fairly significant portion of their time hunting for werewolves. An Elder who spends most of his nights hunting for werewolves is probably neglecting a lot of issues elsewhere. Not to mention that a vampire who spends a significant portion of time in topor (because his soul is off possessing animals or people) risks turning himself into a snack for another vampire. And that's not even getting into the risks of being noticed by a werewolf you're tailing, who ends up using a spirit to tail you back to your body and then kill you or the fact that the bright aura isn't unique to werewolves so a vampire could easily end up tailing some other sort of supernatural being instead.<br /> <br /> Ultimately this seems like anything but &quot;easy.&quot; Could it work? Sure, maybe. But it seems like there's also a very high chance you'd end up with a dead vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-19-2023, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T18:13:14-07:00","id":1512167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512152#post1512152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh. Good thing I specified Shadow Lords - Aura of Confidence renders the Garou's aura unreadable. It's a Gift that has a fairly good chance of going forward into a new edition, since it syncs up with a Vampire mechanic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, in such a case the vampiric detective will have to find the shadow lords by finding other pack members, and then investigate until hopefully finding that one member that seems to not register a specific aura.<br /> <br /> Which means finding a full shadow lords setts will be nightmarish, but that's expected<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512152#post1512152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex 5 kicks you into the Dark Umbra according to W:tA's SOP, so unless they're familiar with ghosts and dead things, it wouldn't necessarily be noticeable... but you also might not be able to keep as close a watch on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure lf that first part, don't they go to the astral umbra instead?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512152#post1512152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That can be fouled with some simple operational precautions that anyone in a conspiracy might use, though. Just don't meet with those people while you're trying to do dirty deeds. At least, not in the waking world; dream communication would be a bit harder to set up, but it would also not be traceable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing to remember is that such a spy could follow the garou day and night, so indeed, the garous are out of vampiric sight in the umbra, but garous do meet each others, and more importantly, they meet their loved ones, which then become blackmail materual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512152#post1512152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this is W5 I was proposing the plan for. That means there are no kinfolk, and they might not even have a caern. Also, you might end up picking up on some actual Fenrir-to-whatever while randomly reading auras, which would potentially throw you off the trail... or place you near a bloodthirsty maniac with no compunctions about tearing you to pieces in the middle of a crowd.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, I was applying non W5 logic<br /> <br /> Howether, it may work by replacing kinfolks with &quot;non garou friends and family&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512152#post1512152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any one can play dirty, and it's not like Garou don't or won't have ways to clamp down on vampires. Bonus: most vampires won't be expecting it if their attention is fixed on werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, it will be dangerous, but it's achievable, and it certainly beat the &quot;don't go into the wood and be paralysed of terror at the though of a lupine going in the city&quot; behavior described in vtm fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T18:35:37-07:00","id":1512170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512167#post1512167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair point, in such a case the vampiric detective will have to find the shadow lords by finding other pack members, and then investigate until hopefully finding that one member that seems to not register a specific aura.<br /> <br /> Which means finding a full shadow lords setts will be nightmarish, but that's expected</div> </div> </div> </div>And they'll probably notice you doing it; Thunder's brood is sneaky like that, and Stormcrows can always be hired to lend a hand.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure lf that first part, don't they go to the astral umbra instead? </div> </div> </div>You're not on the Vampire forum right now, so...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing to remember is that such a spy could follow the garou day and night, so indeed, the garous are out of vampiric sight in the umbra, but garous do meet each others, and more importantly, they meet their loved ones, which then become blackmail materual. </div> </div> </div>You're going to get a rude awakening trying this with the Theurge, whose loved ones are, in large part, spirits. Spirits that quite possibly don't like or even actively hate vampires (they said that Garou might not be out for vampires, but they've not mentioned anything about spirits changing their tack...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My bad, I was applying non W5 logic<br /> <br /> Howether, it may work by replacing kinfolks with &quot;non garou friends and family&quot; </div> </div> </div>It's still up in the air if they can actually have those. At the very least, there's a high probability that they don't meet them anywhere near often enough for you to find out, or have easy to pickup connections due to the effects of Rage on humans. And if they're lupus, they flat out likely won't have the ties that you're looking for. In fact, lupus are going to pick up on your suspicious body language very quickly; they grew up being shadowed and chased constantly for years, they know how to deal with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Indeed, it will be dangerous, but it's achievable, and it certainly beat the &quot;don't go into the wood and be paralysed of terror at the though of a lupine going in the city&quot; behavior described in vtm fluff. </div> </div> </div>Even more achievable is a random lightning strike just popping a snoopy vampire when they're not paying attention to the gathering clouds over head. Bonus: likely Masquerade breach whether you survive or not!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T18:42:35-07:00","id":1512172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512159#post1512159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That actually sounds incredible time intensive and it seems like whoever is doing that would need to spend a fairly significant portion of their time hunting for werewolves</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's time well spent when the reward is the elimination of one of the greatest threat to you and the other kindred of your city/region.<br /> <br /> And vampires are know to dedicate a lot of their tie to specific pursuits, be it politics, thaumaturgical research, or, accordingly spying on others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512159#post1512159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b. An Elder who spends most of his nights hunting for werewolves is probably neglecting a lot of issues elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>An elder would not be the detective, but rather the coordinator, or merely the boss of the detective.<br /> In fact, this task is pretty much the type of thing a prince would demand from a neonate coterie, or a reason to embrace sneaky individuals.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512159#post1512159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Not to mention that a vampire who spends a significant portion of time in topor (because his soul is off possessing animals or people) risks turning himself into a snack for another vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if their body is exposed. With, say, auspex 5, you can leave your body from inside your secure haven, and leave by going through the walls/ceilling.<br /> <br /> It's also mainly a risk if you're alone and in cities/regions with a lack of ruling against diablerie.<br /> <br /> Such a spy could have ghouls, be protected by their sire which would have groomed them specifically to map the local werewolves, be part of a chantry, assamite cell or sabbat pack.<br /> <br /> It's also rarely a problem when you're projecting/possessing during the day, when most vampires are asleep, and then you have as much risk as, well, any vampire since they sleep during the day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512159#post1512159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> And that's not even getting into the risks of being noticed by a werewolf you're tailing, who ends up using a spirit to tail you back to your body and then kill you</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that's the actual risk, but then, it's similar to a human undercover cop spying mafioso. There's an unavoidable risk of being noticed and to meet a certain end while going back home. But it's a necessary risk.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512159#post1512159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> or the fact that the bright aura isn't unique to werewolves so a vampire could easily end up tailing some other sort of supernatural being instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed,. And that's why I precised, after seeing the aura, that the spy should follow the individual to confirm or infirm that they are a werewolf.<br /> <br /> And itf they aren't? It's not a loss, since you identified another supernatural being, making yourself and your boss more knowledgable on what lives or unlives in your city/region.<br /> <br /> In fact, such spying tactic should indeed be used by any vampiric factions or even basically thoughfull vampire individual to map the supernatural around them. Because when you're so focused on survival, you cannot allow yourself to ignore the unknown things around you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512159#post1512159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Ultimately this seems like anything but &quot;easy.&quot; Could it work? Sure, maybe. But it seems like there's also a very high chance you'd end up with a dead vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's easy as in it doesn't takes much ressources or strategy. Yes, the risks are non negligeable, but after all, it's the common fates of vampiric plans. Which often includes a few dead neonates.<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, such a plan could be put in place by a single elder or coterie/pack, embracing specific individuals such as ex cops, or private detectives. Or simply overly curious mortals. You then train them specifically toward the aforementioned disciplines and launch them toward distance spying werewolves.<br /> <br /> You'll probably lose some, but let's not pretend it's a conundrum for elders, neonates can easily be replaced,. Especially if the local prince approves of your plan.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the potential rewards is a bunch of werewolves either dead, blackmailed into backstabing each others, or simply forced to leave due to constant and suddent pressure from police, administration, criminal elements, or the poor kinfolk dominated into stabbing their garou wife in the bed with a silver knife before torching the caern with fire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not saying that garou don't have the means to retaliates or spy back. But that even a moderatly populated and organised kindred city have all the means and motivation to at least try to eliminates the local garou. Which is always better than &quot;don't go into the wood, and pray they don't huff and puff at the elysium's doors&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T19:03:54-07:00","id":1512177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512170#post1512170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And they'll probably notice you doing it; Thunder's brood is sneaky like that, and Stormcrows can always be hired to lend a hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, although I don't know if stormcrows can enter any umbra outqide of the middle one<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512170#post1512170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not on the Vampire forum right now, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>And I wasn't talking about vampire's rules. I also play werewolf and I genuinely don't remember such rules about vampires projecting into the dark umbra. Not saying, you're wrong, but it just seems weird to me, especially when mage's also mention that vampire projects into astral umbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512170#post1512170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going to get a rude awakening trying this with the Theurge, whose loved ones are, in large part, spirits. Spirits that quite possibly don't like or even actively hate vampires (they said that Garou might not be out for vampires, but they've not mentioned anything about spirits changing their tack...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Theurges are no less likely to have flesh and blood loved ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512170#post1512170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still up in the air if they can actually have those. At the very least, there's a high probability that they don't meet them anywhere near often enough for you to find out, or have easy to pickup connections due to the effects of Rage on humans. And if they're lupus, they flat out likely won't have the ties that you're looking for. In fact, lupus are going to pick up on your suspicious body language very quickly; they grew up being shadowed and chased constantly for years, they know how to deal with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough for lupus, but it seems unlikely that W5 garou would not have non garou loved ones. Especially since the few W5 related material, such as the recent visual novel, have such people.<br /> <br /> Plus, even if you indeed have a sept that as a strict &quot;no relations with humans&quot;, it's members will have to interact in some way with humans, even if only to gather information, pay the gang member that stay silent when your pack reunite in the abandonned warehouse,etc people that can then potentially be weaponised against them. And neither of these will be a sept breaker in itself, having your now dominated landlord set fire to your appartement, the gang suddently firing at you when not expected and so on can make your life far more difficult <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512170#post1512170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even more achievable is a random lightning strike just popping a snoopy vampire when they're not paying attention to the gathering clouds over head. Bonus: likely Masquerade breach whether you survive or not!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hardly. A vampire possessing a human or a crow taking enough damage for it's possessed body to die would only enter torpor. And one that is astrally projecting would only have a jumpscare from the sudden noise and light where they're merely spiritually present.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T19:19:10-07:00","id":1512179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512177#post1512177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably, although I don't know if stormcrows can enter any umbra outqide of the middle one</div> </div> </div> </div>They can 1) frequently talk to Garou through the Umbra, and 2) pick out the ugly looking blot that is a vampire in the Umbra, though W5 may handle this differently. And probably way worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I wasn't talking about vampire's rules. I also play werewolf and I genuinely don't remember such rules about vampires projecting into the dark umbra. Not saying, you're wrong, but it just seems weird to me, especially when mage's also mention that vampire projects into astral umbra. </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, it's legacy from the Revised ST Handbook, but that assumes that Vampires are skimming the Dark Umbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Theurges are no less likely to have flesh and blood loved ones. </div> </div> </div>Potentially/likely also guarded by spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fair enough for lupus, but it seems unlikely that W5 garou would not have non garou loved ones. Especially since the few W5 related material, such as the recent visual novel, have such people. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that they wouldn't have any. I said that your stakeout might not be nearly long-term enough to catch them meeting someone they might only see once every few months or per year.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, even if you indeed have a sept that as a strict &quot;no relations with humans&quot;, it's members will have to interact in some way with humans, even if only to gather information, pay the gang member that stay silent when your pack reunite in the abandonned warehouse,etc people that can then potentially be weaponised against them. And neither of these will be a sept breaker in itself, having your now dominated landlord set fire to your appartement, the gang suddently firing at you when not expected and so on can make your life far more difficult </div> </div> </div>Those are also dead giveaways that someone is lazily reading from the Vampire Operations Handbook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hardly. A vampire possessing a human or a crow taking enough damage for it's possessed body to die would only enter torpor. And one that is astrally projecting would only have a jumpscare from the sudden noise and light where they're merely spiritually present.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b </div> </div> </div>There are metaphorical dimensions to that, but I'm not sure how W5 is going to ruin them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T21:01:22-07:00","id":1512184,"title":"","content":"The One thing I love about Kindred succeeding in wiping out the local Garou population is that it means that they just royally screwed themselves over. Without pressure from Garou the Bane and Fomori populations explode, Pentex Subsidiaries start muscling in on all the Ventrue holdings, peoples blood starts tasting worse due to the influences on them, the Nosferatu stop responding to messages because something far worse just took over their Warren.....and why did Geoff's butler just vomit up all his internal organs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T23:49:05-07:00","id":1512188,"title":"","content":"Garou population numbers in urban areas aren't high to begin with. The few that are there are either Bone Gnawers or Glass Walkers. If the Kindred hedged up enough resources and manpower to succeed in a campaign of wiping out the local Garou in the countryside, nothing really noticeable would prop up in the cities itself. <br /> <br /> Maybe the suburban areas, and definitely the rural ones, but urban areas? Again, not that much effect will take place.<br /> <br /> Even if things DO go bad with Banes in Kindred controlled territory, the local prince who had enough power to wipe out the local Garou, can probably comfortably deal with that problem as well. They'd either have Tremere in the city to deal with the Spirits, or any of the other sorcerous bloodlines or clans on contract to help with the matter if no Tremere are present (either Giovanni, even though they frequently specialize with Wraiths from the Low Umbra than Spirits from the Middle Umbra/Spirit Wilds; or maybe the Nagaraja.. but they're very rare; or as a very last resort, the Followers of Set.. but those guys are much more likely to support and entice the growth of Banes to begin with.. so very unreliable for a job on that). <br /> <br /> Fomori would be easier to fight against than Banes, since they are in a physical form and/or has possessed a former mortal. Just either have a Brujah, Gangrel, or Assamite handle them. Venture can pitch in for the fighting (their Fortitude would sure help the war effort) even though they usually dislike getting their hands dirty (but if its antitribu Sabbat Venture, they sure like to fight, don't they? lol). Tzimisce out of all of the aforementioned clans would be the greatest advantage for either a Prince or Archbishop to have (and concerning the former, Tzimisce usually <i>are</i> the Archbishops) to fight against both Banes and Fomori.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T01:20:51-07:00","id":1512193,"title":"","content":"Personally I see it as academic If a vampire is of the wyrm or not. You're talking about an immortal predator which 90 out of a 100 is a complete bastard and of those remaining 10, 9 either have been a murdering scumbag or will degenerate into one. Humans, regular humans have very little reason to tolerate their presence outside of personal interests with werewolves less so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-20-2023, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T02:08:58-07:00","id":1512196,"title":"","content":"This came up in a chat with some buddies; W5's text really doesn't give nature space. The focus is solely on suburbs or urban areas, with very little focus on just outright wilderness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T02:59:46-07:00","id":1512199,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512184#post1512184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The One thing I love about Kindred succeeding in wiping out the local Garou population is that it means that they just royally screwed themselves over. Without pressure from Garou the Bane and Fomori populations explode, Pentex Subsidiaries start muscling in on all the Ventrue holdings, peoples blood starts tasting worse due to the influences on them, the Nosferatu stop responding to messages because something far worse just took over their Warren.....and why did Geoff's butler just vomit up all his internal organs?</div> </div> </div> </div>What? No. From a vampire prespective, Wyrm corporations are exactly the same as regular corporations, they're about as competitive, you don't need the wyrm to have psycho management, and vampires can invest in them just as easily as other corporations. As for blood? In some instances the wyrm will make them taste better, but generally speaking there won't be any significant changes. You should also recognize that Vampires do some environmental engineering of their own for security purposes which encourages the wyrm but vampires in the WoD aren't the virgin hunters in other vampire media and have only been discriminate about blood quality in a few extreme cases (and V5 I guess).<br /> As for Nosferatu being pushed out of their warrens? fat chance. Broadly speaking vampires &gt; Formor, and honestly the Wyld is a bigger threat when it comes to the Ratkin who generally avoid the nos but would be a massive threat if they changed their mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512196#post1512196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This came up in a chat with some buddies; W5's text really doesn't give nature space. The focus is solely on suburbs or urban areas, with very little focus on just outright wilderness.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is a common issue with many of today's writers, they all come from highly cosmopolitan cities and don't really realize that's not how the rest of the world is. Cities (or at least the ones they're thinking of) are home to all kinds of interesting and diverse people worth celebrating while the country is filled with backwards, racist hicks and isn't important in any way, shape or form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-20-2023, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T04:26:59-07:00","id":1512203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512184#post1512184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The One thing I love about Kindred succeeding in wiping out the local Garou population is that it means that they just royally screwed themselves over. Without pressure from Garou the Bane and Fomori populations explode, Pentex Subsidiaries start muscling in on all the Ventrue holdings, peoples blood starts tasting worse due to the influences on them, the Nosferatu stop responding to messages because something far worse just took over their Warren.....and why did Geoff's butler just vomit up all his internal organs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that woudl ever happen<br /> Let's face it, the Garou of pre WW5 not really cleared any city from the Wyrm, not even minimized its effects on the greater scale<br /> Arguably the biggest thing the Garou achieved was the Covenant but even that was Siegfried's, the Ventrue Prince of Vancouver idea; a peace treaty between the local Kindred and the Lupines (In exchange for aiding in reforestation attempts and fighting against resource exploitation, the Lupines would guard his domain from any unwanted intruders and would refrain from unprovoked violence against vampires under Siegfried's protection)<br /> I mean that was HUGE and quite effective while it lasted - aside this the Garou pack's were basically just bio-terrorist, mild anoyance in the grand scheme of things<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu Warrens are fortified underground fortresses not just to provide home to the local Nosferatu but the main line of deffense against the Nictuku and more often than not have their own spawning pools, where vitae is pooled and Animalism utilized to create grotesquely overgrown, fiercely loyal ghoul guardians from subterranean animals \u2013 or from animals that are not traditionally found beneath the city streets, such as crocodiles and other &quot;surprises&quot; <br /> Even the BSD and the Ratkin awoid the Nosferatu warrens<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T11:44:44-07:00","id":1512229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512199#post1512199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What? No. From a vampire prespective, Wyrm corporations are exactly the same as regular corporations, they're about as competitive, you don't need the wyrm to have psycho management, and vampires can invest in them just as easily as other corporations. As for blood? In some instances the wyrm will make them taste better, but generally speaking there won't be any significant changes. You should also recognize that Vampires do some environmental engineering of their own for security purposes which encourages the wyrm but vampires in the WoD aren't the virgin hunters in other vampire media and have only been discriminate about blood quality in a few extreme cases (and V5 I guess).<br /> As for Nosferatu being pushed out of their warrens? fat chance. Broadly speaking vampires &gt; Formor, and honestly the Wyld is a bigger threat when it comes to the Ratkin who generally avoid the nos but would be a massive threat if they changed their mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Broadly speaking, fomori are also typically no match for Garou. But every so often, you get one that's turbo-charged, and while Garou are typically resilient enough to deal with that... well, fomori have a track record of throwing agg around like water just like the werewolves, which vampires don't do so well with, to say the least. Combine that with unexpected psychic powers or being perpetually on fire, and you get a combatant that's an outside context problem, with the outside context creating a situation where the fomor basically just one-shots whatever vampire comes across, because there aren't any ludicrously resilient elders around.<br /> <br /> (Also, the Wyld isn't the greater threat to anyone. It's on the back foot; a few breakthroughs via Thresholds in caerns make it more threatening to Garou and Fera than to vampires.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bThis is a common issue with many of today's writers, they all come from highly cosmopolitan cities and don't really realize that's not how the rest of the world is. Cities (or at least the ones they're thinking of) are home to all kinds of interesting and diverse people worth celebrating while the country is filled with backwards, racist hicks and isn't important in any way, shape or form. </div> </div> </div>I think it's just that they got way too many people who thought that they were writing for Vampire. The entire project, from start to finish, is just an attempt to make Werewolf more like Vampire, because there's some notion that if they make it more like Vampire, it'll be more popular and therefore garner more money, resulting in a project successful by the only metric that a big company cares about.<br /> <br /> It's doomed to fail, of course. This isn't the 90s anymore; Vampire has a pittance of the market share compared to D&amp;D. Hasbro and WotC long ago conspired to get All of The Money in this industry, and they were successful because no one cared about the meager amount of money that's in it, compared to other industries. I doubt that even Hasbro actually cares, but damned if it's not going to try to milk that stone dry of blood even so with the effective monopoly that it enjoys over rpgs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T11:46:43-07:00","id":1512230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512203#post1512203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure that woudl ever happen<br /> Let's face it, the Garou of pre WW5 not really cleared any city from the Wyrm, not even minimized its effects on the greater scale<br /> Arguably the biggest thing the Garou achieved was the Covenant but even that was Siegfried's, the Ventrue Prince of Vancouver idea; a peace treaty between the local Kindred and the Lupines (In exchange for aiding in reforestation attempts and fighting against resource exploitation, the Lupines would guard his domain from any unwanted intruders and would refrain from unprovoked violence against vampires under Siegfried's protection)<br /> I mean that was HUGE and quite effective while it lasted - aside this the Garou pack's were basically just bio-terrorist, mild anoyance in the grand scheme of things<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu Warrens are fortified underground fortresses not just to provide home to the local Nosferatu but the main line of deffense against the Nictuku and more often than not have their own spawning pools, where vitae is pooled and Animalism utilized to create grotesquely overgrown, fiercely loyal ghoul guardians from subterranean animals \u2013 or from animals that are not traditionally found beneath the city streets, such as crocodiles and other &quot;surprises&quot;<br /> Even the BSD and the Ratkin awoid the Nosferatu warrens<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because the Nosferatu are so good at defending against Nictuku. Just ask Baba Yaga, 4th gen and over-statted elder!... oh, wait. You can't. A Nictuku killer her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T18:07:06-07:00","id":1512243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512230#post1512230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, because the Nosferatu are so good at defending against Nictuku. Just ask Baba Yaga, 4th gen and over-statted elder!... oh, wait. You can't. A Nictuku killer her.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> they're indeed good, since after millenias of being hunted by their nemesises, the clan is still there and thriving.<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga was isolated and running from the emss she made in USSR, and the scenario in which she died describe clearly that she wasn't prepared for such a confrontation.<br /> <br /> While the clan as a whole is doing hardly anything but prepare","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T18:20:30-07:00","id":1512245,"title":"","content":"Ok, looks like the prevailing opinion is that Garou and associated Gaian Spirit presence in a city has zero effect on the Wyrms presence or ability to operate. And that vampire operations are unaffected by the presence of BSDs, Fomori, Banes or Pentex acrivities. I'm just going to agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T18:33:35-07:00","id":1512247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512243#post1512243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> they're indeed good, since after millenias of being hunted by their nemesises, the clan is still there and thriving.<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga was isolated and running from the emss she made in USSR, and the scenario in which she died describe clearly that she wasn't prepared for such a confrontation.<br /> <br /> While the clan as a whole is doing hardly anything but prepare</div> </div> </div> </div>She had an Earthbound on retainer via a ghouled Choirister, an immense amount of personal power, reasonably could have backup plans due to pulling Thaumaturgy out of her ass, and still went down. Most Nosferatu are probably surviving because of a low profile, not because they have incredible defenses and a fortified position. Since the Nictuku are all lower generation than the vampires that they're going after, they can probably out-possess all of of a warren's guardian ghoul critterswith Animalism and just Dominate their quarry into standing still and becoming another anticlimax in the annals of the Vampire metaplot.<br /> <br /> And somehow, emulating this setup is supposed to make Werewolf more popular. Go figure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T22:48:33-07:00","id":1512255,"title":"","content":"Yes, Baba Yaga indeed killed the local Nosferatu, no matter how well they were prepared nor how low profile they kept<br /> Thats ture<br /> Likewise how the Clanbooks state, the Nicktuku despite the Warrens, their underground havens were turned into massive fortresses, complete with gun emplacements and embankments on the lower levels AND the Nosferatu information exchange tools, up to and including ShreckNET, to keep up to date with Nictuku sightings... are <i>not enough</i> and Warrens tend to dissapear, found empty with 0 Nosferatu survivors, the Nosferatu could feel their Antediluvian metaphorically breathing down the back of their necks!<br /> Those are also true<br /> But thats make them so damn prepared! They knew all this and try to survive <i>and still around</i>, gather in one place, make Warrens, fortify them, and try to protect each other and their home to the point there is no real difference between the Sabbat Nosferatu and their Camarilla cousins: to the Nosferatu, clan loyalty trumps sect loyalty any night of the week and most of them join out of the sheer pathological fear of their own Antediluvian and the desire to prepare for the last stand against him.<br /> Compared to an Antediluvian and its monstorous children who were ordered to hunt down all of them, their fortresses and preaprations, yes, kind of inadequate<br /> But in the same time, those preparations and fortifications made their Warrens indeed a well guarded frotresses, bunkers and an underground &quot;kingdom&quot; on their own right - places the Ratkin avoid if they can, the Black Spiral Dancers don't really bother them either and no sane Garou pack poke the Nosferatu down there<br /> My point was not about how good against Baba Yaga and the others those fortified Warrens were in the past ten millenium - tho' the Clan indeed survived against all the odds, and not by keeping their numbers low and out of sight, nor by not gathering on one place and make a home - , but the fact, they <i>exist</i> and gives a hard time to everyone who tries to mess with the Nosferatu <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-21-2023, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T01:13:14-07:00","id":1512260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512247#post1512247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She had an Earthbound on retainer via a ghouled Choirister, an immense amount of personal power, reasonably could have backup plans due to pulling Thaumaturgy out of her ass, and still went down. Most Nosferatu are probably surviving because of a low profile, not because they have incredible defenses and a fortified position. Since the Nictuku are all lower generation than the vampires that they're going after, they can probably out-possess all of of a warren's guardian ghoul critterswith Animalism and just Dominate their quarry into standing still and becoming another anticlimax in the annals of the Vampire metaplot.<br /> <br /> And somehow, emulating this setup is supposed to make Werewolf more popular. Go figure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> She no longuer had most of those things, she died alone outside of her hut after being on the run following the fall of her reign over ussr.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T06:15:16-07:00","id":1512280,"title":"","content":"Re: Nosferatu warrens<br /> <br /> They're still guarded by beings that have paper-thin defenses against aggravated damage. I'm surprised that BSDs don't just pour napalm down and light it on fire, given that they tend to live for scorching the earth and poisoning whatever's left.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512260#post1512260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She no longuer had most of those things, she died alone outside of her hut after being on the run following the fall of her reign over ussr.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>She still had her Generation and high stats, which would put her on par with all of the Nictuku. That at least allows her to fight without being Dominated into complacence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T12:56:39-07:00","id":1512295,"title":"","content":"Generally the world makes a lot more sense when you give vampires 1st edition aggravated rules: They can't soak fire, sunlight or faith with stamina, and these cause aggravated wounds. They can soak teeth, claws and magic blades, and these cause aggravated wounds. Aggravated wounds wasn't about whether it can be soaked or not, but how much of a bitch it was to heal. <br /> <br /> Also while BSDs and Ratkin have good access to resist toxin and won't be killed by poison air it should be noted that vampires don't need air at all. Nosferatu in particular have infinite endurance and Potence and can access areas and hiding spots that enemies wouldn't be able to access without very specific powers or a concerted effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T14:05:01-07:00","id":1512300,"title":"","content":"I've been glossing over things... has anyone actually gotten enough leaks about W5 to actually see how vampires and werewolves are going to stack up, or is all this just relitigating decades old debates about vampire vs werewolf conflicts in the WoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T14:41:16-07:00","id":1512306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512300#post1512300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been glossing over things... has anyone actually gotten enough leaks about W5 to actually see how vampires and werewolves are going to stack up, or is all this just relitigating decades old debates about vampire vs werewolf conflicts in the WoD?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing explicit. However:<br /> <br /> 1: IIRC there was a stated goal that 5th edition would re-approach the big 3 with the aim to make them more compatible with one another. <br /> <br /> 2: despite most often being argued as the weakest splat, vampires got neutered, with a strong focus on out-of-control fledglings. Disciplines got weakened, factions got flanderized, elders walked out. Given what we already know about werewolves (Umbra more distant, more human character concepts with ordinary jobs, Fianna losing their virility-cult and GoF becoming evil because they were gigachads...) and the general disdain for elder werewolves/traditions we've seen... yeah, they're getting neutered too. <br /> <br /> I would be very, very surprised if werewolves had more than a few slight advantages over vampires. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T14:58:17-07:00","id":1512307,"title":"","content":"I... really don't see how any of that explains the last three pages of the thread. How did, &quot;WoD5 is meant to be more crossover capable,&quot; turn into debates about Baba Yaga's story in a fashion that's actually relevant to W5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T15:00:29-07:00","id":1512308,"title":"","content":"You expect a thread to go on for more than 10 pages and remain entirely on topic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T15:50:09-07:00","id":1512312,"title":"","content":"Let's get this back on track:<br /> <br /> Who wins in a fight between the Followers of Set, the Black Spiral Dancers and House Balor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T20:26:22-07:00","id":1512327,"title":"","content":"Do the Balor Sidhe have Naming or Sovereign? Cos...that'll do it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nah theres not much more info out currently, though there have been some whispers by former writers of W5 that more info will see the light of day soon....maybe not info certain parties want to see the light of day......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T03:42:44-07:00","id":1512344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512312#post1512312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's get this back on track:<br /> <br /> Who wins in a fight between the Followers of Set, the Black Spiral Dancers and House Balor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you call on allied factions in escalation.<br /> <br /> Currently my monies on nwo when they're sent in to clean up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T04:48:58-07:00","id":1512347,"title":"","content":"[Double post]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-23-2023, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T04:49:55-07:00","id":1512348,"title":"","content":"Setites, based on no logic except personal bias. -<br /> Tying in Wolves vs Leeches and W5: If the Garou don't have issues with vampires anymore, and vampires need to kill to make the beast shut up now, does that mean there's a potential for the &quot;Let's have another Impergium&quot; faction to be buddies with humanity's predators? At least for the time being (I mean, it doesn't really work because vampires both cultivate humanity and profit off of civilization, but I could see some kind of alliance between some factions based on the shared thread of &quot;humans must be brought to heel and kept under careful control.&quot; An unplayable one that violates the way you're supposed to play WoD5 I think)<br /> <br /> Also, in retrospect, the mysterious lack of hostility explains my confusion from one of the V5 books that had a plot where you find a confused and terrified fourteen year old after her first change and take her to her people. I kept waiting for the part with the fuzzy murder party and kinfolk with stakes and fire, but the writing kept talking like this was a totally normal thing to happen in the WoD. Makes so much more sense now...<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T10:48:25-07:00","id":1512368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512196#post1512196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This came up in a chat with some buddies; W5's text really doesn't give nature space. The focus is solely on suburbs or urban areas, with very little focus on just outright wilderness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but thinking about it I have a similar issue with how in the beginning the Introduction rightly starts with &quot;Werewolf is also a game about spirituality. Each of the World of Darkness games provides a different perspective or set of truths it considers to be incontrovertible, and for Werewolf, those truths are animistic.\u200b&quot; That's why the war against the Wyrm is the centerpiece of the game. The biggest wrong in the world that needs to be corrected is spiritually represented by the Wyrm. That's how the Garou look at it. And yet... doesn't it feel like the descriptions in the text are more focused on the idea of how Garou should stop bad humans from doing bad stuff in a very broad sense (while applying a very human perspective, though)? The animistic worldview should be more important than just broadly turning Garou into activists and rebels concerned with mundane politics. Not that you can't bring those things into a WtA-game but to keep the flavor of the game the presentation should look at those things through the lens of the game's animistic worldview as well as the Garou's cultural investment in that worldview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T00:14:42-07:00","id":1512408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1508634-w5-to-be-released-august-31-pre-ordens-open-preview-coming-this-thursday?p=1512312#post1512312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's get this back on track:<br /> <br /> Who wins in a fight between the Followers of Set, the Black Spiral Dancers and House Balor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, lets unplack this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> White room scenario with 1v1v1?<br /> Or specific number, age, time period, rank ,etc?<br /> Too many variable in the equation to have a proper answer to that one<br /> But probably the Setite; with the humble Presence 3 (Entrancement - makes someone obsessively want to please them) make the BSD in love with you and <i>ask</i> it to kill the Balor member. Then give it a belly rub, scratch behind the ear and a doggy treat<br /> Or the three probably wont even fight just would go to the nearest 